{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XxGm4zCJEh3XtHbK7ckCvF","type":"tool_result","content":"400\t- Acceleration `T.skateAccel` 300 × `(1 − 0.6 (v/vmax)²)` along the stick. Gliding with no input decelerates by\n401\t  `T.iceGlide` 28.\n402\t- **Turning**: the velocity heading rotates toward the stick direction at `lerp(T.turnSlow 5.0, T.turnFast 2.6,\n403\t  v/vmax)` rad/s. The sideways component of velocity relative to the facing decays at `T.edgeGrip` 6/s, which gives\n404\t  carves rather than slides.\n405\t- **Hockey stop**: when the stick points more than 120° from the velocity at speed > 60, the skater enters `stop`\n406\t  (at least 0.22 s): deceleration `T.stopDecel` 700, a snow spray (event `stop`), the torso turned 70°. The skater then\n407\t  accelerates the new way.\n408\t- Facing follows velocity (the AI may skate backward at 0.75× speed to keep facing the puck, using C-cut legs).\n409\t- **Turbo** meter 0..1: drains `T.turboDrain` 0.45/s while held and moving, and regenerates `T.turboRegen` 0.18/s\n410\t  once released for 0.6 s.\n411\t- **Bodies**: r 7. Masses: heroic 1.0, bulky 1.35, goalie 1.6 (The Vault 2.2). Skater–skater overlap pushes them\n412\t  apart with a restitution of .3. A collision without the check state is a \"bump\": no knockdown unless the closing\n413\t  speed is above `T.accidentalHit` 180.\n414\t- **Boards**: reflect the normal velocity × .3 and keep 85% of the tangential. Faster than 120 into the boards: a\n415\t  \"rattle\" event (sound, glass shake).\n416\t\n417\t### 7.3 The puck (`Puck`)\n418\t- r 1.6, drawn as a black ellipse of 3×2 px with a 1-px highlight, plus a shadow. Above 300 u/s it gets a streak; the\n419\t  **Puck trail** setting chooses Off, Streak or Glow (neon).\n420\t- Free motion: `v −= (T.puckFriction 26 + T.puckDrag 0.12 × |v|) dt`. Gravity 700 in the air. Hitting the ice: vz ×\n421\t  −0.3, and speed × 0.9 when vz was below −60. Speed cap 760.\n422\t- **4 substeps** per step, each a swept test against: the boards (restitution `T.boardBounce` .62 normal, .92\n423\t  tangential; the glass .5 when z > 17); posts (.82 plus a **ping** event; the crossbar when z is 19–21 inside the\n424\t  mouth); the net (from behind or the sides .2, a \"net\" sound); goalies (section 7.6); sticks (pickup or deflection);\n425\t  bodies (r 7: .35, a \"body\" event; a shot hitting a skater is a **block**). Over the glass top, or through a\n426\t  shattered panel: **out of play**, then a faceoff at the nearest end-zone dot.\n427\t- **Goal**: the puck's center crosses the goal line inside the mouth (`|y − C.y| < 16 − 1.6`) with z < 20 − 1.6,\n428\t  moving inward. The puck stays in the net (`inNet`; the bulge plays).\n429\t- **Possession**: the owner's blade point is `pos + R(facing) · [11, hand × 4]` (`hand` +1 right shot, −1 left, from\n430\t  the player data). The puck eases toward the blade at k = 30/s and weaves ±3 across (`sin(t × 9)`) at low speed.\n431\t- **Pickup**: a loose puck within `T.pickupRadius` 8 × the handling multiplier of the blade point (or 10 of the body\n432\t  center), at z < 6, after the skater's `pickupCooldown` (0.25 s once it releases the puck). If the relative speed is\n433\t  under 300 it is taken. Faster, it is caught with chance `clamp(1.3 − rel/450 + 0.08 (Hnd − 3), 0.1, 1)`, otherwise\n434\t  it deflects off the blade (reflected around the blade's normal at 0.5×).\n435\t- **Puck battles**: when opposing blades are both within 8 of a loose or carried puck, every 0.2 s the one with the\n436\t  higher `Hnd + Hit/2 + RNG.sim() × 3` takes it (a \"battle\" event, stick-clack sounds).\n437\t\n438\t### 7.4 Passing\n439\t- **Target**: the teammate whose bearing is nearest the aim within 75°; otherwise the nearest teammate ahead; with\n440\t  mouse or right-stick aim, the teammate nearest the reticle within 80, otherwise a pass to the space at the reticle.\n441\t- **Lead**: aim at `mate.pos + mate.v × tFlight × 0.9`, iterated twice; speed `clamp(220 + 0.9 d, 240, 420) ×\n442\t  (0.9 + 0.033 Pas)`; angular error σ = `0.06 × (1.3 − 0.1 Pas)` rad.\n443\t- **Interception**: an opponent's blade that comes within 8 of the puck's path tries a pickup (7.3).\n444\t- **Saucer pass** (`lob`): `E.arc` with apex 10 and speed × 0.8. It can't be intercepted while z > 6, lands near the\n445\t  mate and wobbles on landing.\n446\t- **Receiving**: the pass sets `receiving` on the target. The CPU turns to it; a lone human's control switches to the\n447\t  receiver at once (auto-switch, standard in hockey games).\n448\t- **One-timer**: a receiver who presses shoot while a pass is on its way and within 0.35 s of arriving, or who holds\n449\t  shoot when it arrives, fires on contact: speed = the slap formula at charge .85 × `T.oneTimerBonus` 1.15, and the\n450\t  aim error halves. The prompt `{shoot} ONE-TIMER!` pops over the human receiver while the pass flies.\n451\t- **Call for pass**: a human without the puck whose CPU teammate carries it presses `pass`; the carrier passes to\n452\t  them within 0.3 s if the lane is clear, otherwise as soon as it opens (up to 1.2 s). The human's indicator flashes\n453\t  \"!\".\n454\t\n455\t### 7.5 Shooting\n456\t- `shoot` with the puck: released within 0.18 s it is a **wrist shot**: `T.wristSpeed` 330 × shot multiplier\n457\t  (`0.85 + 0.05 Sht`), lift 2–10 at the goal, error σ 5 × (1.3 − 0.1 Sht). Held longer it is a **slapshot**: the\n458\t  skater winds up (slowed to 0.6×; a meter fills over `T.slapCharge` 0.9 s; a poke or check can strip it). On release:\n459\t  speed `(T.slapBase 380 + T.slapGain 160 × charge) × shot multiplier`, lift 4–18, σ `7 × (1.3 − 0.1 Sht) × (1.4 −\n460\t  0.4 charge)`.\n461\t- **The aim point in the net**: without aim input, the open side (the side farther from the goalie's center) at mid\n462\t  height. With stick aim, up and down on the stick pick near or far side (mirrored for each attack direction). With the\n463\t  mouse, where the reticle's line meets the mouth. Slapshots go **top shelf** (z 14–18) when the goalie is down.\n464\t- Turbo adds +12% speed, the Lumber item gives +30% and zero error, and KABOOM turns a charge ≥ .95 into a **KABOOM\n465\t  shot** (7.10).\n466\t- Every shot is logged with type (`wrist`, `slap`, `onetimer`, `kaboom`, `deke`, `rebound`, `deflect`), speed and\n467\t  distance. \"On goal\" means the shot's line crosses the goal line inside the mouth. Shots from anywhere count\n468\t  (dump-ins too).\n469\t\n470\t### 7.6 Goalies (`Goalie`)\n471\t- **Positioning**: on an arc in front of the goal center, radius 10–26 (out to 26 to cut the angle when the puck is\n472\t  far, back to 10 when it is close), on the bisector toward the puck. Lateral speed `T.goalieLateral` 150 × (0.85 +\n473\t  0.05 Rfx), with T-push bursts to 230. When the puck is behind the net, the goalie hugs the post on the puck's side.\n474\t  Idle animations: tapping the posts, a crouch bounce.\n475\t- **Save solver**: whenever the puck's line will cross the goal line inside the mouth within 1 s (a shot, pass or\n476\t  deflection), predict the crossing `(yc, zc, tc)`. After a reaction delay (`T.goalieReact` 0.16 − 0.015 (Rfx − 3) +\n477\t  difficulty offset, plus 0.08 if **screened** by a body within 14 of the shot line, plus 0.12 if **deked** within the\n478\t  last 0.5 s at under 70 range), the goalie moves toward `yc`, picks a save type and, when the puck crosses the\n479\t  goalie's plane, tests its **save shape**. All widths scale with `0.9 + 0.033 Size` × the item and boss factors:\n480\t  - standing: `|dy| < 8`, z 0–22;\n481\t  - butterfly (zc < 9): `|dy| < 14`, z 0–10, plus the upper body `|dy| < 6`, z 10–20;\n482\t  - glove (high, catching side) and blocker (high, other side): a reach disc of r 5 out to `dy ±15`, z 10–21;\n483\t  - stack (desperation, needs `|dy| > 12` in under 0.2 s): `|dy| < 18`, z 0–8, then 1 s to get up.\n484\t- **Outcome**: glove saves freeze (`T.gloveCatch` 0.55; then a whistle and a faceoff in that zone). Pad and blocker\n485\t  saves **rebound** at 0.35 v, ±50° away from the net. Butterfly saves: 40% smother, 60% rebound. Rebounds are live.\n486\t- **Poke check**: when a carrier comes within 22 in front, a 40% (× Rfx) chance to strip the puck.\n487\t- **Kaboom blast**: a KABOOM shot that hits a goalie blows them back (`blasted`, 1.2 s, flailing into the net). With\n488\t  `T.kaboomBlast` 0.6 the puck carries through (a goal); otherwise it drops dead in the crease.\n489\t- **Manual goalie** (shootout only, for the defending human): the stick moves along the arc and in or out; ✕\n490\t  butterfly, □ poke, ○ stack toward the stick. Glove and blocker reach is automatic within the standing shape.\n491\t- **Balance targets** (checked by `tests/balance.mjs`, 18.4): wrist shots from more than 150 away saved 88–96%;\n492\t  one-timers across the crease 40–60%; breakaway dekes 45–65%; KABOOM shots on target 20–40% saved.\n493\t\n494\t### 7.7 Checking, the glass, grudges (`Hits`)\n495\t- `shoot` without the puck starts `check` (0.3 s): a lunge of +60 along the facing and a shoulder-lead pose.\n496\t- **Contact** with a rival (r 8 each) during `check`: `impulse = T.checkPower 1.0 × (closing speed + 60) × (attacker\n497\t  mass / target mass) × (0.8 + 0.067 Hit) × (turbo 1.45) × (KABOOM 2.0) × (Poutine 1.6)`.\n498\t  - Below 90: **bump**. The target staggers 0.25 s; a carrier loses the puck 50% of the time.\n499\t  - 90 up to `T.knockdown` 150: **check**. The target stumbles 0.5 s and loses the puck.\n500\t  - 150 and up: **BIG HIT**. The target is knocked down (`down` for 1.4 s: a tumble, then a belly slide at 0.8 ×\n501\t    impulse along the normal, then `getup` 0.5 s). Hit-stop 0.07 s, a shake of 3, a zoom punch to 1.1, the crowd\n502\t    goes \"OHHH\", BOOM +18, and the target's grudge against the hitter +35.\n503\t- **The glass**: a body sliding or knocked into the boards faster than `T.glassCrack` 170 cracks the panel there. If\n504\t  the panel was already cracked, or the speed is over `T.glassShatter` 240, it shatters: shards (`bits` in light blue\n505\t  and white), a crash, the front-row fans flinch, BOOM +8 or +15, and the commentary calls it. A shattered panel lets\n506\t  the puck out. At the next stoppage two glass techs skate out and put a new panel in (1.5 s, cosmetic).\n507\t- **Accidental contact** knocks the referee or the mascot over too (comedy). Goalies can be knocked down only by a\n508\t  KABOOM check (the crowd boos).\n509\t- **Grudge** (per ordered pair, 0..100): +35 for being big-hit, +10 for being checked, +15 for being chirped, +10\n510\t  when the rival big-hits a teammate. It decays 4/s after 3 s of peace.\n511\t\n512\t### 7.8 Deke and poke\n513\t- **Deke** (`deke` with the puck): 0.45 s, a sideways cut of +90 toward the stick (alternating when the stick is\n514\t  neutral), a spin animation (a spin-o-rama with turbo). Checks in its first 0.3 s miss with chance `0.7 + 0.04 (Hnd −\n515\t  3)`. Cooldown 0.8 s. A goalie within 70 \"bites\" (7.6). A deke that leaves a defender behind within 1 s is a\n516\t  `deke_beat` event (BOOM +6, commentary).\n517\t- **Poke** (`deke` without the puck): 0.35 s, the blade reaches 18 ahead. If it passes within 8 of a carried puck,\n518\t  steal chance is `T.pokeBase 0.55 + 0.08 (pokerHnd − carrierHnd)`. A miss leaves the poker off balance for 0.3 s.\n519\t\n520\t### 7.9 Chirping (`chirp`)\n521\tPressing chirp makes the skater shout a line from `TEXT.chirps` at the nearest rival within 120: a speech bubble (2 s,\n522\ttiny font, wrapped to 90 px) and babble in their voice. BOOM +3; the target's grudge +15; cooldown 4 s. CPU skaters\n523\tchirp after big hits and goals (30%), and the human's chirps raise the chance that a CPU rival with Fight ≥ 4\n524\tchallenges.\n525\t\n526\t### 7.10 The BOOM meter and KABOOM mode (`Boom`)\n527\t- **One meter per team**, 0..100, × `T.boomGain` 1.0. Gains: big hit +18, check +6, glass crack +8 or shatter +15,\n528\t  fight win +45, fight loss +5, goal +20, shot on goal +4, save (to the goalie's team) +5, completed pass +2,\n529\t  one-timer +6, deke beat +6, chirp +3, BOOM Box item +40, mascot down +10, perfect Flood Wagon +30, Doris's organ\n530\t  (chapter 5) +30.\n531\t- **At 100 → KABOOM** for `T.kaboomTime` 15 s, or until the other team scores. A screen flash, an explosion burst over\n532\t  the team's bench, \"KA-BOOM!\" (title font, shaking), the arena lights tint the team's color with a pulse, flame\n533\t  cannons in the Dome, and the music's `kaboom` layer fades in (drums and distorted bass). For that team: infinite\n534\t  turbo, the slapshot charges 2× faster, a full charge fires a **KABOOM shot**, checks are 2× strong, skates throw\n535\t  sparks and leave molten `melt` trails, and their goalie reacts 0.03 s faster. The meter then resets to 0.\n536\t- **KABOOM shot**: 760 u/s with zero error. The puck is a fireball (a glowing sprite, fire particles every step, a light\n537\t  following it). Into the goalie → the blast (7.6). Into a skater → an explosion and a knockdown. Into the boards → an\n538\t  explosion, and a hit panel shatters. A KABOOM goal: the net tips back in an explosion, a confetti and fire burst, a\n539\t  double horn and fireworks in the Dome.\n540\t- **Gilded Mode** is the Grizzlies' KABOOM (chapter 5): the same rules with gold flames.\n541\t\n542\t### 7.11 Fights and the sin bin (`Fight`)\n543\t- **Trigger**: a human-controlled skater within 40 of a rival when either holds a grudge ≥ 40 against the other gets\n544\t  the prompt `HOLD {lob} — DROP THE GLOVES`. Holding △ for 0.5 s challenges. A CPU rival accepts with\n545\t  `clamp(0.4 + 0.12 (Fgt − 3) + grudge/200, 0.1, 0.95)` (forced in chapter 3 when the Bruise Brothers are involved).\n546\t  A human rival (local or online) gets `HOLD {lob} TO ACCEPT` for 3 s. Declining is **turtling**: the decliner's team\n547\t  BOOM −10 and the challenger's +10, and the crowd boos. A **CPU** with Fgt ≥ 4 and grudge ≥ 70 near a human-controlled\n548\t  skater challenges them the same way. At most one fight per 60 s of clock and `T.fightMax` 3 per game.\n549\t- **Staging**: a whistle; the clock stops; the camera moves to `brawler`, zoom 1.6, framing the two (`cam.frame`).\n550\t  Gloves and helmets drop as sprites on the ice; the other skaters circle at 50; the referee and the linesman hover;\n551\t  the crowd stands; the organ plays the fight vamp. The fight HUD shows two portraits with balance and stamina bars.\n552\t- **Fighters**: balance 100 (`T.fightBalance`) and stamina 100 (regen 25/s); damage × `0.8 + 0.067 Fgt`.\n553\t  - **Jab** (✕): 0.25 s, 6 damage, 8 stamina, staggers 0.12 s (rig: `jab`).\n554\t  - **Haymaker** (□): wind-up 0.35 s (a clear telegraph: the arm draws back, a glint), active 0.1, recover 0.35. 18\n555\t    damage (+6 if held up to 0.6 s), 22 stamina. A whiff leaves you open for 0.5 s (rig: `haymaker`, or `hook`\n556\t    alternating).\n557\t  - **Duck** (○): 0.35 s, immune to haymakers and half damage from jabs; 10 stamina; cooldown 0.4 (pose: `crouch` +\n558\t    lean back).\n559\t  - **Yank** (△): 0.3 s. If it lands, the rival's guard breaks for 0.6 s and they lose 15 stamina. **Three yanks\n560\t    within 4 s pull the jersey over their head** (their rig gets `hood: true` in jersey color): blind for 1.5 s.\n561\t  - With no stamina, everything is 40% slower.\n562\t  - The CPU fighter ducks a haymaker wind-up with probability = its skill, and otherwise mixes jabs, haymakers and\n563\t    yanks by personality.\n564\t- **End**: balance ≤ 0 → that fighter falls (`down`); the winner raises a fist (`cheer`); a crowd roar; the winner's\n565\t  team BOOM +45. The loser goes to the **sin bin** for `T.sinBin` 20 s of play clock (a \"POWER PLAY\" banner and timer\n566\t  under the score bug), seated in the box, then steps out through the box door. If 20 s pass, the linesmen separate\n567\t  them: a draw with no penalty and BOOM +10 each. Play resumes with a faceoff at the nearest dot.\n568\t\n569\t### 7.12 Fan throws, power-ups and hazards (`Items`)\n570\t- **Throws**: every `T.itemEvery` 25–45 s of play, and 25% of the time right after a big hit or goal, a fan in the\n571\t  stands throws (a lob arc from the crowd over the glass) onto the neutral or attacking zone. The item slides to a stop\n572\t  and lasts 12 s (blinking for its last 3). Arena pools are in 11.2.\n573\t- **Pickup**: a skater body within 12. Icons and timers show over the holder's head.\n574\t\n575\t| Item | Look | Effect |\n576\t|---|---|---|\n577\t| HOT SAUCE | red bottle (store `bottle`) | infinite turbo 8 s, fire trail |\n578\t| GRANDMA'S TAPE | white tape roll | 10 s: can't lose the puck to pokes or checks below a big hit; passes can't be intercepted |\n579\t| POUTINE | bowl of fries (store `bowl`) | 10 s: can't be knocked down; every check is a big hit (×1.6) |\n580\t| LUMBER | a stick with a lightning bolt | the next 3 shots: +30% speed, zero error |\n581\t| BRICK PADS | a brick | the holder's goalie grows ×1.35 for 12 s |\n582\t| BOOM BOX | a boombox | +40 team BOOM |\n583\t| HOT COCOA (pond only) | a steaming thermos | turbo refilled + 20% speed 8 s |\n584\t\n585\t| Hazard | Where | Effect |\n586\t|---|---|---|\n587\t| OCTOPUS | Grindhouse, Dome, cheat | a slip patch r 10: skaters crossing it `slip` (1.2 s, legs up, a slide); at the next stoppage the referee picks it up and twirls it overhead |\n588\t| RUBBER RAT | Grindhouse | scurries randomly for 10 s; trips skaters (as slip) |\n589\t| HATS | after any hat trick | 20–40 hats rain from the stands (cosmetic, swept up at the stoppage) |\n590\t\n591\t- **AI item greed**: a CPU skater not involved in the play (not the carrier, its marker or the pressure player)\n592\t  detours to an item within 120 (`T.aiItemGreed`).\n593\t- **Arena hazards**:\n594\t  - **Thin ice** (pond): 3 elliptical patches (40 × 24) at fixed spots outside the creases, each with integrity 100.\n595\t    A knockdown on a patch costs 50 and a big hit there 100. At 0 the patch breaks into a hole: black water, ripples\n596\t    and a splash. A skater who enters a hole is `frozen` for 3 s (rig tinted icy blue inside a translucent block),\n597\t    then pops out at the edge. A puck that falls in is lost, then a faceoff. Holes refreeze (as a darker patch) after\n598\t    30 s or at intermission.\n599\t  - **Snowbanks** (pond): the boards are snowbanks with no glass. Restitution .3 and a snow puff. A big hit into one\n600\t    leaves the target `buried` for 1.5 s with only the head and skates showing.\n601\t  - **Polar Pete** (mall): the mascot skates figure eights in the neutral zone during play. A moving obstacle (mass\n602\t    1.5) that can be checked (\"MASCOT DOWN!\", BOOM +10); it gets up after 3 s and waves.\n603\t  - **Discount Drop** (mall): every 40 s a ceiling claw lowers a crate to center ice; it breaks into a power-up.\n604\t\n605\t### 7.13 Team AI (`AI`)\n606\t- **Cadence**: each CPU skater re-thinks every `lerp(0.3, 0.12, skill)` s and reacts after `lerp(0.35, 0.1, skill)`\n607\t  s; between decisions it steers. Steering: seek the target, stay 12 from the boards unless chasing the puck, keep 40\n608\t  from teammates, and avoid rivals while carrying.\n609\t- **With the puck** (offense):\n610\t  - **Carrier**: shoot when in the shooting zone (within 200 of the net, within ±60° of its axis, at most one body in the\n611\t    lane), or when a one-timer pass is on. Pass when pressured (a rival within 26 ahead) or when a teammate is clearly\n612\t    better placed (open lane, at least 60 closer to the net). Deke when a defender is square in front within 30 (40%\n613\t    × Hnd/3). Otherwise carry toward the net, slaloming around defenders, with turbo in open ice.\n614\t  - **Support forward**: get open on the far side at the dot height (about 150 from the goal line); once the carrier\n615\t    crosses the blue line, drift to the far post or the slot for a one-timer.\n616\t  - **Point**: stay at the blue line as an outlet; crash the net for rebounds when aggression is high.\n617\t- **Without the puck** (defense):\n618\t  - **Pressure**: the nearest skater intercepts the carrier's position 0.3 s ahead, then checks (when Hit ≥ 3 and\n619\t    `RNG.sim() < aggression`) or pokes.\n620\t  - **Cover**: marks the most dangerous rival without the puck (in the passing lane, or between them and the net).\n621\t  - **Home**: guards the slot between the puck and its own net.\n622\t- **Loose puck**: each team sends the skater who can reach the predicted puck position first. The rest take offense or\n623\t  defense spots according to which team will probably win the race.\n624\t- **Faceoffs**: centers face off at the dot; wingers line up on both sides; the point man behind.\n625\t- **Difficulty** (Settings): Rookie, Pro, All-Star, Legend set AI skill .35 / .55 / .75 / .95, CPU goalie reaction\n626\t  offsets +.06 / +.02 / 0 / −.02 s, and the human team's goalie −.03 / −.01 / 0 / +.01. Light rubber-banding (CPU\n627\t  skill −.1 while it leads by 3 or more) on Rookie only.\n628\t- **Teammates of humans** use the same AI and also obey call-for-pass. Team tactics from story choices: **Finesse**\n629\t  (pass bias +30%, speed +4%) or **Grit** (check bias +30%, BOOM gain +15%).\n630\t\n631\t### 7.14 Match flow (`Match`)\n632\t- **Configuration**: `{ home, away, arena, periods: 3, periodLen: 120, ot: 'sudden' (120 s, 3-on-3) | 'none',\n633\t  shootout: true, intros: true, replays: 'auto', flood: 'ask' | 'always' | 'never', difficulty, cheats, objectives,\n634\t  script, humans: [{ team, input }] }`.\n635\t- **Phases**: `intro` → `faceoff` → `play` ⇄ `stoppage` → `goal` → `replay` → `faceoff` … `periodEnd` →\n636\t  `intermission` (Flood Wagon) → `faceoff` … `final` → `results`. Also `fight`, `ot`, `shootout` and `celebration`.\n637\t  The clock counts down only in `play`. The engine's pause freezes everything.\n638\t- **Faceoff**: the referee holds the puck, raises an arm and drops it after a random 0.6–1.2 s. Each center presses\n639\t  `pass` or `shoot` when it drops; the earlier press within 0–0.25 s after the drop wins (a press before the drop is a\n640\t  slow, mistimed swipe); a CPU center reacts after its skill delay. The winner's swipe sends the puck back to a\n641\t  teammate.\n642\t- **Stoppages**: a frozen puck, the puck out of play, after a fight, at the end of a sin-bin call. Each brings a\n643\t  whistle, a 1.5 s pause, a lower-third stat card (shots, hits, faceoffs %), an organ sting, and then the faceoff.\n644\t- **Goals**: the horn (3 s), the red goal light spinning behind that net, the team's goal song sting, the crowd jumping,\n645\t  the scorer's celebration (chosen by personality: fist pump, sniper aim, knee slide, stick guitar, a bounce off the\n646\t  glass), and teammates converging. \"GOAL!\" in the title font, the scoring summary (scorer and assists, the\n647\t  last two touches by the scorer's team), then an **instant replay** (7.16), then a center faceoff.\n648\t- **Hat trick**: a player's third goal makes hats rain, and the commentary calls it. **Hoser Hat Trick**: one player\n649\t  with a goal, an assist and a fight win in one game, shown as a toast.\n650\t- **Periods**: the buzzer at 0:00, then the period summary card. **Intermission**: the Flood Wagon minigame (offered\n651\t  per the `flood` option; skipping runs a 6 s AI resurfacing fast-forward), then the next period. Teams switch ends\n652\t  every period.\n653\t- **Overtime**: sudden death; a tie after it goes to the shootout (exhibition and story). In session mode: at most 60\n654\t  s of sudden death, then a tie.\n655\t- **Shootout**: 3 rounds each (home first), then sudden-death rounds. A shooter starts at center with the puck and an\n656\t  8-second shot clock; the attempt ends on a shot, a save, a goal, or the puck going backward. Humans shoot for their\n657\t  team (the skaters rotate) and play goalie against the CPU's shooters (6.1). The HUD shows big ✓ and ✗ marks.\n658\t- **Final**: the final horn, the winning team celebrates, the losers slump (`kneel`), then **results**.\n659\t- **Stats** per skater: goals, assists, shots, hits, big hits, takeaways, fights won, turbo used, top shot speed.\n660\t  Per goalie: saves and shots against. Per team: everything summed, plus BOOM filled and Kabooms.\n661\t- **Three stars**: rank players by `3 G + 2 A + 0.5 bigHits + 1.5 fightsWon + 0.3 shots` (goalies:\n662\t  `0.12 saves + 2 × (save% − .85) × 10`) and announce the third, second and first stars, each with a portrait card and a\n663\t  commentary line.\n664\t- **Objectives**: declarative `{ id, text, on: 'goal' | 'hit' | …, where(e, match) }` counters plus a `need`, checked\n665\t  live. A star toast when one is met.\n666\t\n667\t### 7.15 Camera director (`Cam`)\n668\t- **Play**: focus on the puck (or carrier) plus a lead of 0.25 s of puck velocity. If a lone human's skater is more\n669\t  than 220 from the puck, shift 25% toward them. With several local humans, `cam.frame([puck, ...humans],\n670\t  { margin: 60, zoom: [.78, 1] })`. `cam.smooth` .15; bounds from `map.bounds(view)`.\n671\t- **Zoom**: 1.0 (Settings → Camera distance: Near 1.15, Normal 1.0, Far 0.85); 1.15 at faceoffs; a 1.1 punch on big\n672\t  hits (0.3 s); out to 0.85 briefly when the puck flies faster than 400.\n673\t- **Fights**: `brawler`, zoom 1.6, framing the fighters. **Celebrations**: 1.3 on the scorer. **Intros**: a dolly\n674\t  along the lineup. **Replays**: 7.16. Then back to the player's camera setting (Broadcast `threequarter` or Overhead\n675\t  `topdown`, cycled by the `camera` action and saved).\n676\t\n677\t### 7.16 Instant replay (`Replay`)\n678\t- **Recorder**: every second step, push `{ puck, skaters and goalies: { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, rigState }, events }`\n679\t  into an 8 s ring buffer. `rigState` is the object passed to `rig.update`, so the replay re-poses rigs exactly.\n680\t- **Goal replay**: once the celebration has played for 1.5 s, cut (a puck-shaped wipe) to the last 4 s before the goal\n681\t  at 0.5× in the `brawler` view following the puck at zoom 1.25, with letterbox bars, a \"REPLAY\" bug, and the\n682\t  recorded events re-firing their effects. ✕ (or confirm) skips. Setting: Replays Auto or Off. Big-hit and Kaboom\n683\t  replays (3 s) also play at the next stoppage when Replays is Auto: when such an event happens, copy its clip (2 s\n684\t  before to 1 s after) out of the ring buffer, because the buffer will have moved on by the stoppage.\n685\t- **Highlights**: keep the 3 best clips of a story run (goal type and hit power score them) in memory for the end\n686\t  credits.\n687\t\n688\t### 7.17 Commentary (`Talk`)\n689\t- **Booth**: CHUCK WALLOP (play-by-play) and MOOSE PLUNKETT (color), with live portraits (rigs in suits) in a bottom\n690\t  subtitle box. Two lines at most; non-modal, auto-advancing (`talk.say(text, { modal: false, auto: 2.4, portrait,\n691\t  name })`).\n692\t- **Selection**: each event type has a pool (`TEXT.talk[type]`) with priority and cooldowns: a global 1.2 s, the\n693\t  same line 120 s, the same type 6 s. Goals, fights, Kabooms and glass breaks interrupt; filler (Moose's anecdotes)\n694\t  only plays after 8 s of quiet play. Variables: `{name} {team} {victim} {goalie} {score} {arena} {period}`.\n695\t- **Voices**: every line babbles (10.1) in the speaker's voice. Settings: Commentary On/Off, Subtitles On/Off,\n696\t  Voices volume.\n697\t- **Tips** (Coach Marge) are separate: a banner just below the score bug with glyph chips, shown the first time its\n698\t  trigger fires per save profile (Appendix D).\n699\t\n700\t### 7.18 HUD (`Hud`; it keeps clear of `game.cornerArea()` and inside a 92% title-safe area)\n701\t- **Score bug** (top center, about 200 × 30): team logo chips, abbreviations, scores at font scale 2, the period\n702\t  (`1ST 2ND 3RD OT SO`), the clock `m:ss`, and under each team its BOOM meter (80 × 4; flames and a countdown while in\n703\t  KABOOM).\n704\t- **Power play** strip under it: `POWER PLAY MUK 0:14`, with the sin-binned player's tag.\n705\t- **Player markers**: a colored ring decal under each human's skater (P1–P4 in `E.PLAYER_COLORS`, the seat colors\n706\t  online), a chevron with `P1` above, and an arrow on the screen edge when they are off screen. A turbo bar (16 × 2)\n707\t  under the chevron. The shot meter above the shooter while charging (gold when full).\n708\t- **Radar** (bottom right, about 108 × 48): the rink outline, skaters as team-colored dots, humans as larger dots with\n709\t  rings, the puck white.\n710\t- **Prompts** (bottom center, above the subtitles): context chips (`{shoot} ONE-TIMER!`, `HOLD {lob} DROP THE GLOVES`,\n711\t  `{pass} SKIP`).\n712\t- **Banners**: GOAL!, SAVE!, POST!, BIG HIT!, THROUGH THE GLASS!, KA-BOOM!, FIGHT!, POWER PLAY, HAT TRICK!, PERIOD\n713\t  2, FINAL, in the title font with shake and color cycling (honoring reduce motion).\n714\t- **Fight HUD**: two portraits with bars at the top corners, and the fight control chips at the bottom.\n715\t- **Lower-thirds** at stoppages: one broadcast-style stat card for 3 s.\n716\t\n717\t---\n718\t\n719\t## 8. Art direction\n720\t\n721\t**Base**: the engine's native look (`res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`, HD Humanoids at size 1.2–1.3, lit scenes, shaded with\n722\t`E.tones`, props, particles), aimed at Symphony of the Night and Metal Slug quality, as AI_GUIDE asks. Act on every\n723\tlook note from `tools/check.mjs`.\n724\t\n725\t- **Skaters**: build `heroic` at size 1.2 (enforcers `bulky` at 1.3). Long-sleeved jersey (`outfit: 'shirt'`,\n726\t  `sleeves: 'long'`, `colors.cloth` the jersey, `trim` the stripe), breezers in `pants`, socks in the team color, skates,\n727\t  big gloves (`glove`), a hockey helmet, number and letter, `weapon: 'stick'`, and shoulder pads (`armor: true`, plate\n728\t  in the jersey color). Hair shows under the helmet (some flow, mullets on the Lumberjacks). Beards come from a darker\n729\t  skin tone on the jaw: add a `beard` color option if needed and log it.\n730\t- **Goalies**: `bulky` at 1.3 (The Vault 1.75), pads, blocker, catcher, mask, `gstick`, and pad and mask colors per\n731\t  team.\n732\t- **Referees**: `heroic` at 1.15, white shirt with black stripes, orange armbands (`trim`), a black helmet, a whistle\n733\t  (one dot).\n734\t- **Crowd**: as in the SPORTS kit: two small fans per stand tile (4 × 5 shirt, 3 × 3 head), colored 70% home and 30%\n735\t  away, swaying. Excitement drives them: claps, standing, jumping on goals, hands on heads after a big hit, a wave\n736\t  around the arena when quiet for 20 s. Fans hold signs (tiny-font text: `BARN BURNER`, `KABOOM!`, `MARGE 4 PM`,\n737\t  `SAVE THE ICEBOX`, `PIPESY ♥`). Behind each net, 4–6 bigger **glass pounders** (Humanoid at size 0.9 in the classic\n738\t  style) bang the glass when play comes near. On the near side, a row of dark head-and-shoulder silhouettes is drawn\n739\t  in screen space along the bottom edge when the camera is low (the broadcast foreground).\n740\t- **Team logos**: a 24 × 24 string sprite each (`E.sprite` rows plus a palette of 4–6 colors), used at center ice (×3),\n741\t  in the score bug (scaled down to 12 or 16), on menu cards (×3) and on bench banners. Section 11.1 describes them.\n742\t- **Effects**: ice spray on stops and turns (white `dust` and `bits`); a skate shower when someone is hit; glass shards;\n743\t  a puck streak; a slapshot shockwave ring; KABOOM fire, explosions and sparks; steam from melt; snow (weather) at the\n744\t  pond; confetti; hats; an octopus splat; a flying tooth on a big fight punch (a white bit, \"chiclets\"); dizzy stars\n745\t  circling a knocked-down head; sweat drops in fights; turbo speed lines.\n746\t- **Lighting**: canvas lights in every arena (11.2 lists them). Goal lights pulse red behind the net. KABOOM tints the\n747\t  arena. Spotlights sweep during intros and the title.\n748\t- **UI style**: dark blue-black panels (`E.ui.box` gradients) with ice-white text and a gold accent (`#ffd36a`),\n749\t  with team colors on cards. Theme the engine's HTML screens with `new E.Shell(game, { theme })` in the same colors and\n750\t  a large font: body text at least 24 CSS px at 1080p (check a screenshot).\n751\t\n752\t---\n753\t\n754\t## 9. Animation (the engine's procedural rigs plus new hockey motion)\n755\t\n756\tHockey motion is added by **wrapping `rig.solvePose`** on each skater and goalie rig (`Rigs`). It overrides feet,\n757\tknees, hips, torso lean, hands and stick joints (`E.ik3` for knees and elbows) from a small state the Skater passes\n758\tin (`skate: { phase, push, lean, stop, back, cross }`, `stick: { blade: [f, s, z], top, follow }`). Fights, cheers and\n759\tfalls use the engine's own `attack` moves, `pose`, `down` and `flip`. Every animation below must play in all three views.\n760\t\n761\t| Motion | How |\n762\t|---|---|\n763\t| Skating stride | Phase advances by `speed / 22`. Each foot pushes back and out diagonally (3 o'clock or 9 o'clock), then recovers under the hip. Knees bend 35°, hips drop 2.5, the torso leans .35 rad (.5 with turbo). The free arm swings when not stick-handling |\n764\t| Glide | Feet parallel, knees soft, a slight sway |\n765\t| Crossovers | Turning hard at speed: the outside foot crosses over in front, alternating |\n766\t| Hockey stop | The torso turns 70° off the velocity, both blades skid sideways with a deep knee bend, a spray at the feet |\n767\t| Backward C-cuts | The hips swing, the feet trace C shapes (AI defenders only) |\n768\t| Stick-handling | The blade weaves ±3 in front; the hands follow (the top hand at the hip, the bottom hand 40% down the shaft) |\n769\t| Pass / saucer | The blade sweeps back to front toward the target; a saucer flicks up at the end |\n770\t| Wrist shot | Weight shift, a fast sweep, a high follow-through |\n771\t| Slapshot | Wind-up (the stick rises behind the shoulder and holds while charging), downswing to the ice, follow-through pointing at the target |\n772\t| One-timer | A short wind-up already held, then the strike on contact |\n773\t| Deke | Spin-o-rama (a 360° body spin with `flip`-like twist), toe drag (the blade pulls the puck back across) |\n774\t| Check | The shoulder leads (lean into it), the stick across the chest |\n775\t| Hit reaction / fall | A stagger (bump); `down` + `flip` tumble + a belly slide (big hit); squashed against the glass (`rig.kick(-.4)`) when hit into it; `getup` from a kneel |\n776\t| Poke | The stick shoots forward along the ice in a lunge |\n777\t| Slip | Feet fly up, landing on the back, a spin-slide (octopus, rat) |\n778\t| Goalie | A ready crouch (pads together, glove up), shuffle and T-push, butterfly (knees down, pads flared), glove and blocker saves, pad stack, poke, covering the puck, celebrating, blasted (flailing backward into the net) |\n779\t| Faceoff | Centers crouch with sticks down; the referee raises an arm and drops the puck; the swipe |\n780\t| Celebrations | Fist pump, sniper aim (the stick held like a rifle), knee slide, stick guitar, bouncing off the glass, a team huddle |\n781\t| Fights | Gloves off (sprites fall), circling in `stance: 'guard'`, one hand gripping the rival's jersey (the hand held at the rival's shoulder), `jab`, `haymaker` and `hook` from `E.MOVES`, a duck, jersey over the head (`hood`), the knockdown, the winner's `cheer` |\n782\t| Bench and coach | Spares sit (a sit pose via solvePose: hips at bench height, knees forward); Coach Marge gestures (`wave`, `hips`) |\n783\t| Story set pieces | The handshake line (two lines sliding past, hands out), the Cup lift (`cheer` with the Cup sprite held at the hands), the Flood Wagon driver seated and steering, Polar Pete's dance (a bulky white rig, a big round head from an extra ball drawn over it, ears), the organist playing (hands bobbing on the beat via `audio.onBeat`) |\n784\t\n785\t**Animation lab** (`#lab`, also in the Dev panel): one skater, one goalie and one referee on a small rink, a list of\n786\tevery motion above, a slider for speed and phase, and a `brawler` / `threequarter` / `topdown` toggle. Film each\n787\tmotion with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` (`--seed 1`) and check: the wind-up, the strike, the settle, no snaps or backward\n788\tsweeps.\n789\t\n790\t---\n791\t\n792\t## 10. Audio (all synthesized in code; no audio files)\n793\t\n794\t### 10.1 Voices: babble (Animalese/Simlish style)\n795\t- `Synth.babble(text, voice, { onLetter })` turns a line into syllables. Each letter that sounds (vowels, and\n796\t  consonants as onsets) is a 55–85 ms blip: a `pulse` or `saw` source through two bandpass filters at the vowel's\n797\t  formants (a: 800/1200 Hz, e: 500/1900, i: 300/2300, o: 500/900, u: 350/700; consonants borrow the next vowel and add\n798\t  a 10 ms noise click for `s t k p` sounds). Pitch is the voice's base × (a letter-hash offset of ±3 semitones). `!`\n799\t  raises the last 4 syllables by 4 semitones; `?` glides the last syllable up; `,` and `.` add 120 / 220 ms pauses.\n800\t  It runs on the engine's new `voice` bus.\n801\t- A voice is `{ base: Hz, range: semitones, speed: syllables/s, wave, formantShift, gruff (noise mix) }`. Marge: low,\n802\t  gruff, slow. Dunny: mid and bright. Snipes: high and fast. Lou: very low, soft and slow. Lemmy: mid and wobbly\n803\t  (vibrato). Glitterman: nasal (formants × 1.15), fast. Chuck: mid-high, very fast. Moose: low and gruff. The referee\n804\t  barks single syllables. The crowd's chant mixes 6 voices.\n805\t- It hooks into `E.Dialog` through the voice hook (section 4) for cutscenes and the booth, and into chirp bubbles,\n806\t  intros (\"Number NINE… DUNNY… MACPHAIL!\"), the referee's calls and crowd chants. Its randomness comes from `RNG.fx`\n807\t  so it never changes the simulation.\n808\t\n809\t### 10.2 Sound effects (`audio.define` voices; custom graphs where noted)\n810\tSkate stride swish (filtered noise, pitch by speed, one per push); hockey stop \"shhhk\" (noise, a bandpass sweep down);\n811\tpuck on stick \"tock\"; pass \"thwap\"; wrist shot \"snap\"; slapshot crack plus whoosh; one-timer (a louder crack); **post\n812\t\"PING\"** (triangle 1850 Hz, 0.9 s decay, a slight detune: the most recognizable sound in hockey); crossbar ping (2100\n813\tHz); puck on boards (a low thud and a rattle); puck on glass (a sharp clack and a ring); net swish; body check thump\n814\tplus a babble \"oof\"; big hit (a deeper thump, a glass rattle, crowd \"OHHH\"); glass crack (a sharp tick) and glass\n815\tshatter (a noise burst and a descending sine tinkle cluster of 12 voices); the referee's whistle (a two-tone pea\n816\twhistle with vibrato); **the goal horn** (a custom graph: 3 detuned `brass` oscillators at 98, 147 and 196 Hz through\n817\tthe lowpass `lp: 900`, 0.25 s attack, 2.6 s hold, then release, plus noise \"air\"); the period buzzer (square at 220 Hz,\n818\t1.5 s); punches (a thud and a whoosh); dizzy stars twinkle; power-up pickup (an arpeggio); item throw (a whoosh);\n819\toctopus \"splort\"; KABOOM explosion (engine `explode` + a sub-bass drop); the Flood Wagon engine (a looped low saw\n820\tputter, pitch by speed), its horn \"A-OOGA\"; menu move, select and back (soft organ blips).\n821\t\n822\t### 10.3 Crowd and organ\n823\t- **Crowd bed**: two looped noise sources (bandpass 400 Hz and 1.2 kHz, an LFO swell) whose gain follows\n824\t  `Crowd.excitement` (0..1: raised by shots, near misses, hits, goals; decays). Plus reactions: \"OHHH\" (a swell\n825\t  sweeping down), \"AHHH\" (a near miss), cheer (a burst with high-voiced babble), boo (low, filtered babble), the\n826\t  \"KA-BOOM!\" chant (6-voice babble on the beat, with claps), and claps in rhythm.\n827\t- **The organ** (`organ` wave, a Leslie-like vibrato of 6 Hz at .004): original stings only. A rising charge fanfare\n828\t  (G4 C5 E5 G5 – E5 G5), a chromatic walk-up vamp for faceoffs, a clap-along vamp (\"da-da-da da-da\"), a sad trombone\n829\t  slide for an opponent's penalty, a fight vamp (minor and tense), and a goal sting per team. In the Ol' Icebox, Doris\n830\t  the organist plays them visibly. **Never copy existing chants or songs** (no \"Charge!\" bugle call, no stadium rock\n831\t  standards).\n832\t\n833\t### 10.4 Music (engine song format; the new `organ` and `brass` waves; named layers)\n834\t| Song | Use | Character |\n835\t|---|---|---|\n836\t| `theme` | title, attract | arena chip-rock anthem: saw power chords, a driving square lead, drums; the \"Ice Hoc-Kaboom\" hook |\n837\t| `menu` | menus, setup | a relaxed loop from the theme's chords |\n838\t| `locker` | cutscenes (locker room) | gritty bass and a snare shuffle, organ pads |\n839\t| `pond` | pond cutscenes, the pond arena's stoppages | a folksy pulse-wave fiddle tune in 6/8 |\n840\t| `grind` | Grindhouse | a punk loop |\n841\t| `mall` | MegaMall | cheesy synth-pop |\n842\t| `final` | Dome cutscenes, the final | epic, brass |\n843\t| `play` | under play (quiet) | a low pulse plus layers `drive` (in the third period and OT), `kaboom` (KABOOM mode), `fight` (fights) |\n844\t| `flood` | the Flood Wagon minigame | an original skaters' waltz (3/4, organ) |\n845\t| `victory`, `defeat` | results | a fanfare, a sad trombone |\n846\t| `credits` | the end credits | the theme as a ballad, then full band |\n847\t| goal stings ×6 | one per team | 2 bars over the horn |\n848\t\n849\t**Mix**: buses `music` (setting), `sfx` (setting), `voice` (setting: Voices) and the crowd (on sfx, plus its own\n850\tsetting: Crowd). Duck the music under the commentary voice (−4 dB) and in the pause menu (the engine does this).\n851\t\n852\t---\n853\t\n854\t## 11. Content\n855\t\n856\t### 11.1 Teams (3 skaters + 1 goalie each; ratings 1–5: Spd / Sht / Pas / Hit / Fgt / Hnd; goalies Rfx / Size / Reb)\n857\t| Team | Abbr | Home dark / away white trim | Logo (24×24) | Players |\n858\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n859\t| **Mukluk Falls Muskrats** | MUK | brown `#5a3a22`, gold `#e8b43a`, cream `#f3e6c8` | a buck-toothed muskrat face in a gold ring | #9 Duncan \"Dunny\" MacPhail, C, playmaker 4/3/5/3/2/4, shoots L · #19 Priya \"Snipes\" Sandhu, sniper 5/5/3/2/2/5, R · #44 Lou \"Big Lou\" Beaudoin, enforcer D (bulky) 2/4/2/5/5/2, R · G #31 Lemmy \"The Sieve\" Kowalchuk 3/4/3 (trait: **Talks to Posts**: 20% of goals within 4 of a post ring off it instead) |\n860\t| **Dryfork Drillers** | DRY | black `#1d1d22`, orange `#f07a1a` | an oil derrick with a drop | #7 \"Rig\" McCoy, C 3/3/4/3/3/3 · #15 \"Gusher\" Gomez 4/4/3/2/2/4 · #2 \"Drill Bit\" Dobbs, D 3/2/2/4/3/2 · G #35 Derrick Okafor 2/3/2 |\n861\t| **Logjam Lumberjacks** | LOG | red plaid `#b3262a` + black, cream | a bearded log face | #10 Axel Sundqvist, C 3/4/3/3/3/3 · #27 \"Sawdust\" Sally Lindgren 4/4/3/3/2/4 · #88 \"Big Timber\" Thibodeau, enforcer (bulky) 2/3/2/5/4/2 · G #1 \"Stumpy\" O'Rourke 3/4/3 |\n862\t| **Grindhouse Bruise Brothers** | GRD | purple `#4b2a6b`, lime `#9be04a` | a fist inside a gear | #66 Rocco Bruiser (bulky) 3/3/2/5/5/2 · #67 Rollo Bruiser (bulky) 3/3/2/5/5/2 · #12 \"Mumbles\" Malone 4/4/3/2/3/4 · G #29 \"Tank\" Tankersley 3/5/2 |\n863\t| **Megaplex Marauders** | MEG | teal `#18b5b0`, magenta `#e0389a` | a shopping cart flying a pirate flag | #23 Chad Glitterman, C 4/3/4/2/1/4 · #8 \"Zoom\" Zhang 5/3/3/2/2/4 · #5 \"Promo\" Perkins, D 3/3/3/4/3/3 · G #40 \"Kiosk\" Kingsley 4/3/4 |\n864\t| **Gilded Grizzlies** | GLD | gold `#d9a520`, black `#141414`, white | a grizzly head in a crown | #1 Sterling Glitterman Jr. 5/5/4/3/2/5 (**Golden Twister**) · #91 \"Silk\" Sullivan 4/3/5/2/2/5 · #55 \"Brick\" Brickowski (bulky) 3/4/2/5/5/2 · G #00 **The Vault** 5/5/5 (boss: size 1.75) |\n865\t\n866\t- **Rating multipliers**: speed `0.85 + 0.05 Spd`; shot speed `0.85 + 0.05 Sht`, shot error `1.3 − 0.1 Sht`; pass\n867\t  speed `0.9 + 0.033 Pas`; check `0.8 + 0.067 Hit`; fight damage `0.8 + 0.067 Fgt`; pickup radius `0.85 + 0.05 Hnd`.\n868\t  Goalie reaction `−0.015 (Rfx − 3)`, save shapes × `0.9 + 0.033 Size`, freeze chance `+0.06 (Reb − 3)`.\n869\t- **Golden Twister** (Sterling): in the offensive zone, 1 in 3 carries end in a 0.6 s spin with a golden glow\n870\t  (telegraphed), then a curving shot (spin 1.2, like the SPORTS kit's curl) that cuts the CPU goalie's save chance by\n871\t  25%. Checking him during the spin is a guaranteed big hit and BOOM +10.\n872\t- **The Vault**: size 1.75; the first two KABOOM shots only stagger him (\"VAULT LOCKED\"). After the second, \"THE\n873\t  VAULT IS CRACKED!\": size 1.4 and Rfx −1 for the rest of the game. Weak to cross-crease one-timers (lateral speed ×\n874\t  0.8) and dekes (he bites 1.5×).\n875\t- **Coach and staff portraits**: Coach Marge Pelletier (grey bun, cardigan, whistle), Old Gus (90, cap, the Flood\n876\t  Wagon driver), Doris (organist, beehive hair), Goldie Glitterman (gold fur coat, sunglasses), Polar Pete (mascot),\n877\t  and Chuck and Moose (suits; Moose is missing teeth).\n878\t\n879\t### 11.2 Arenas\n880\t| Arena | Chapter | Look | Lights | Items | Hazard | Music |\n881\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n882\t| **The Ol' Icebox** (Mukluk Falls) | 1, title, practice | wooden barrel-vault beams, string lights, 1962 championship banners, wooden stands, fans in toques, Doris's organ booth, a hand-painted scoreboard, ads (`MUKLUK MUFFLER & TIRE`, `KOWALCHUK'S PEROGIES`, `BAIT 'N' BAGELS`) | ambient .65 warm, 6 hanging lamps over the ice (light radius 260) | Hot Sauce, Tape, Poutine, BOOM Box | – | organ, `play` |\n883\t| **Lake Kabonk** (pond) | 2 | a frozen lake at dusk, snowbank boards, pines, two cabins with lit windows, a bonfire with fans in parkas, string lights on poles, snowmen (store) | ambient .45 blue dusk, bonfire flicker, cabin windows, string lights; weather snow .5 | Hot Cocoa, Tape, Lumber, BOOM Box | thin ice ×3, snowbanks | `pond` |\n884\t| **The Grindhouse** | 3 | a steel-truss mill arena, chain-link above the end boards, steam pipes, rowdy stands, a cage-match vibe, ads (`RUSTBELT SCRAP`, `IRON GUT CHILI`) | ambient .5 cool green, flickering fluorescents (`RNG.fx`), steam vents | Poutine, Lumber, BOOM Box | octopus throws after goals, rubber rats | `grind` |\n885\t| **MegaMall Ice Palace** | 4 | a rink in a mall atrium: storefront neon, escalators, a fountain, a food court, ads on every inch (`GLITTERMAN MEGAPLEX — COMING SOON!`) | ambient .7, neon emissives in magenta and teal, fountain glow | Discount Drop crates (any item) | Polar Pete, Discount Drop | `mall` |\n886\t| **The Kaboom Dome** | 5 | a huge arena: gold-trimmed boards, flame cannons in the corners, laser lights, fireworks, a sold-out crowd, a jumbotron frame on replays | ambient .55, strong white ceiling lights, moving spotlights in intros, flame light on goals and Kabooms | Hot Sauce, Brick Pads, BOOM Box | octopus (rare), Gilded Mode | `final` |\n887\t\n888\tEvery arena uses the same rink geometry. Walls, stands and props come from the TileMap (`types` for tiers with `face`\n889\tmaterials), `r.shape` / `E.SHAPES` (new entries: `locker`, `bench-box`, `organ`, `net`, `glass-crew-cart`,\n890\t`flood-wagon`, `flame-cannon`, `cabin`, `fountain`, `escalator`, `storefront`, `scoreboard`, `kaboom-cup`) and\n891\t`r.prop` (lamps, banners, signs, torches as bonfire, trees).\n892\t\n893\t### 11.3 Story: THE CUP RUN\n894\t\n895\t**Premise**: Mukluk Falls (pop. 812) has one thing: the Ol' Icebox, a 1950s barn where the town learned to skate.\n896\tDeveloper Goldie Glitterman bought the land and plans a \"Megaplex Parking Experience\". Coach Marge digs up **Town\n897\tBylaw 1897-B**: *any rink that houses the Kaboom Cup shall stand forever.* So the Muskrats, a ragtag team of three\n898\tskaters, a superstitious goalie and a 72-year-old coach, have to win the regional Kaboom Cup: five games, five\n899\tbarns, five rivals. **Tone**: a small-town sports-movie comedy told like a hockey broadcast, with hockey clichés"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de63938e-b4cc-4b63-8e8c-4cc91a6c7b2f","uuid":"5ed93b26-f37a-4cfa-8e98-f80ada415952","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:51:07.996Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-055058__x9a2bbb/work/PLAN.md","content":"- Acceleration `T.skateAccel` 300 × `(1 − 0.6 (v/vmax)²)` along the stick. Gliding with no input decelerates by\n  `T.iceGlide` 28.\n- **Turning**: the velocity heading rotates toward the stick direction at `lerp(T.turnSlow 5.0, T.turnFast 2.6,\n  v/vmax)` rad/s. The sideways component of velocity relative to the facing decays at `T.edgeGrip` 6/s, which gives\n  carves rather than slides.\n- **Hockey stop**: when the stick points more than 120° from the velocity at speed > 60, the skater enters `stop`\n  (at least 0.22 s): deceleration `T.stopDecel` 700, a snow spray (event `stop`), the torso turned 70°. The skater then\n  accelerates the new way.\n- Facing follows velocity (the AI may skate backward at 0.75× speed to keep facing the puck, using C-cut legs).\n- **Turbo** meter 0..1: drains `T.turboDrain` 0.45/s while held and moving, and regenerates `T.turboRegen` 0.18/s\n  once released for 0.6 s.\n- **Bodies**: r 7. Masses: heroic 1.0, bulky 1.35, goalie 1.6 (The Vault 2.2). Skater–skater overlap pushes them\n  apart with a restitution of .3. A collision without the check state is a \"bump\": no knockdown unless the closing\n  speed is above `T.accidentalHit` 180.\n- **Boards**: reflect the normal velocity × .3 and keep 85% of the tangential. Faster than 120 into the boards: a\n  \"rattle\" event (sound, glass shake).\n\n### 7.3 The puck (`Puck`)\n- r 1.6, drawn as a black ellipse of 3×2 px with a 1-px highlight, plus a shadow. Above 300 u/s it gets a streak; the\n  **Puck trail** setting chooses Off, Streak or Glow (neon).\n- Free motion: `v −= (T.puckFriction 26 + T.puckDrag 0.12 × |v|) dt`. Gravity 700 in the air. Hitting the ice: vz ×\n  −0.3, and speed × 0.9 when vz was below −60. Speed cap 760.\n- **4 substeps** per step, each a swept test against: the boards (restitution `T.boardBounce` .62 normal, .92\n  tangential; the glass .5 when z > 17); posts (.82 plus a **ping** event; the crossbar when z is 19–21 inside the\n  mouth); the net (from behind or the sides .2, a \"net\" sound); goalies (section 7.6); sticks (pickup or deflection);\n  bodies (r 7: .35, a \"body\" event; a shot hitting a skater is a **block**). Over the glass top, or through a\n  shattered panel: **out of play**, then a faceoff at the nearest end-zone dot.\n- **Goal**: the puck's center crosses the goal line inside the mouth (`|y − C.y| < 16 − 1.6`) with z < 20 − 1.6,\n  moving inward. The puck stays in the net (`inNet`; the bulge plays).\n- **Possession**: the owner's blade point is `pos + R(facing) · [11, hand × 4]` (`hand` +1 right shot, −1 left, from\n  the player data). The puck eases toward the blade at k = 30/s and weaves ±3 across (`sin(t × 9)`) at low speed.\n- **Pickup**: a loose puck within `T.pickupRadius` 8 × the handling multiplier of the blade point (or 10 of the body\n  center), at z < 6, after the skater's `pickupCooldown` (0.25 s once it releases the puck). If the relative speed is\n  under 300 it is taken. Faster, it is caught with chance `clamp(1.3 − rel/450 + 0.08 (Hnd − 3), 0.1, 1)`, otherwise\n  it deflects off the blade (reflected around the blade's normal at 0.5×).\n- **Puck battles**: when opposing blades are both within 8 of a loose or carried puck, every 0.2 s the one with the\n  higher `Hnd + Hit/2 + RNG.sim() × 3` takes it (a \"battle\" event, stick-clack sounds).\n\n### 7.4 Passing\n- **Target**: the teammate whose bearing is nearest the aim within 75°; otherwise the nearest teammate ahead; with\n  mouse or right-stick aim, the teammate nearest the reticle within 80, otherwise a pass to the space at the reticle.\n- **Lead**: aim at `mate.pos + mate.v × tFlight × 0.9`, iterated twice; speed `clamp(220 + 0.9 d, 240, 420) ×\n  (0.9 + 0.033 Pas)`; angular error σ = `0.06 × (1.3 − 0.1 Pas)` rad.\n- **Interception**: an opponent's blade that comes within 8 of the puck's path tries a pickup (7.3).\n- **Saucer pass** (`lob`): `E.arc` with apex 10 and speed × 0.8. It can't be intercepted while z > 6, lands near the\n  mate and wobbles on landing.\n- **Receiving**: the pass sets `receiving` on the target. The CPU turns to it; a lone human's control switches to the\n  receiver at once (auto-switch, standard in hockey games).\n- **One-timer**: a receiver who presses shoot while a pass is on its way and within 0.35 s of arriving, or who holds\n  shoot when it arrives, fires on contact: speed = the slap formula at charge .85 × `T.oneTimerBonus` 1.15, and the\n  aim error halves. The prompt `{shoot} ONE-TIMER!` pops over the human receiver while the pass flies.\n- **Call for pass**: a human without the puck whose CPU teammate carries it presses `pass`; the carrier passes to\n  them within 0.3 s if the lane is clear, otherwise as soon as it opens (up to 1.2 s). The human's indicator flashes\n  \"!\".\n\n### 7.5 Shooting\n- `shoot` with the puck: released within 0.18 s it is a **wrist shot**: `T.wristSpeed` 330 × shot multiplier\n  (`0.85 + 0.05 Sht`), lift 2–10 at the goal, error σ 5 × (1.3 − 0.1 Sht). Held longer it is a **slapshot**: the\n  skater winds up (slowed to 0.6×; a meter fills over `T.slapCharge` 0.9 s; a poke or check can strip it). On release:\n  speed `(T.slapBase 380 + T.slapGain 160 × charge) × shot multiplier`, lift 4–18, σ `7 × (1.3 − 0.1 Sht) × (1.4 −\n  0.4 charge)`.\n- **The aim point in the net**: without aim input, the open side (the side farther from the goalie's center) at mid\n  height. With stick aim, up and down on the stick pick near or far side (mirrored for each attack direction). With the\n  mouse, where the reticle's line meets the mouth. Slapshots go **top shelf** (z 14–18) when the goalie is down.\n- Turbo adds +12% speed, the Lumber item gives +30% and zero error, and KABOOM turns a charge ≥ .95 into a **KABOOM\n  shot** (7.10).\n- Every shot is logged with type (`wrist`, `slap`, `onetimer`, `kaboom`, `deke`, `rebound`, `deflect`), speed and\n  distance. \"On goal\" means the shot's line crosses the goal line inside the mouth. Shots from anywhere count\n  (dump-ins too).\n\n### 7.6 Goalies (`Goalie`)\n- **Positioning**: on an arc in front of the goal center, radius 10–26 (out to 26 to cut the angle when the puck is\n  far, back to 10 when it is close), on the bisector toward the puck. Lateral speed `T.goalieLateral` 150 × (0.85 +\n  0.05 Rfx), with T-push bursts to 230. When the puck is behind the net, the goalie hugs the post on the puck's side.\n  Idle animations: tapping the posts, a crouch bounce.\n- **Save solver**: whenever the puck's line will cross the goal line inside the mouth within 1 s (a shot, pass or\n  deflection), predict the crossing `(yc, zc, tc)`. After a reaction delay (`T.goalieReact` 0.16 − 0.015 (Rfx − 3) +\n  difficulty offset, plus 0.08 if **screened** by a body within 14 of the shot line, plus 0.12 if **deked** within the\n  last 0.5 s at under 70 range), the goalie moves toward `yc`, picks a save type and, when the puck crosses the\n  goalie's plane, tests its **save shape**. All widths scale with `0.9 + 0.033 Size` × the item and boss factors:\n  - standing: `|dy| < 8`, z 0–22;\n  - butterfly (zc < 9): `|dy| < 14`, z 0–10, plus the upper body `|dy| < 6`, z 10–20;\n  - glove (high, catching side) and blocker (high, other side): a reach disc of r 5 out to `dy ±15`, z 10–21;\n  - stack (desperation, needs `|dy| > 12` in under 0.2 s): `|dy| < 18`, z 0–8, then 1 s to get up.\n- **Outcome**: glove saves freeze (`T.gloveCatch` 0.55; then a whistle and a faceoff in that zone). Pad and blocker\n  saves **rebound** at 0.35 v, ±50° away from the net. Butterfly saves: 40% smother, 60% rebound. Rebounds are live.\n- **Poke check**: when a carrier comes within 22 in front, a 40% (× Rfx) chance to strip the puck.\n- **Kaboom blast**: a KABOOM shot that hits a goalie blows them back (`blasted`, 1.2 s, flailing into the net). With\n  `T.kaboomBlast` 0.6 the puck carries through (a goal); otherwise it drops dead in the crease.\n- **Manual goalie** (shootout only, for the defending human): the stick moves along the arc and in or out; ✕\n  butterfly, □ poke, ○ stack toward the stick. Glove and blocker reach is automatic within the standing shape.\n- **Balance targets** (checked by `tests/balance.mjs`, 18.4): wrist shots from more than 150 away saved 88–96%;\n  one-timers across the crease 40–60%; breakaway dekes 45–65%; KABOOM shots on target 20–40% saved.\n\n### 7.7 Checking, the glass, grudges (`Hits`)\n- `shoot` without the puck starts `check` (0.3 s): a lunge of +60 along the facing and a shoulder-lead pose.\n- **Contact** with a rival (r 8 each) during `check`: `impulse = T.checkPower 1.0 × (closing speed + 60) × (attacker\n  mass / target mass) × (0.8 + 0.067 Hit) × (turbo 1.45) × (KABOOM 2.0) × (Poutine 1.6)`.\n  - Below 90: **bump**. The target staggers 0.25 s; a carrier loses the puck 50% of the time.\n  - 90 up to `T.knockdown` 150: **check**. The target stumbles 0.5 s and loses the puck.\n  - 150 and up: **BIG HIT**. The target is knocked down (`down` for 1.4 s: a tumble, then a belly slide at 0.8 ×\n    impulse along the normal, then `getup` 0.5 s). Hit-stop 0.07 s, a shake of 3, a zoom punch to 1.1, the crowd\n    goes \"OHHH\", BOOM +18, and the target's grudge against the hitter +35.\n- **The glass**: a body sliding or knocked into the boards faster than `T.glassCrack` 170 cracks the panel there. If\n  the panel was already cracked, or the speed is over `T.glassShatter` 240, it shatters: shards (`bits` in light blue\n  and white), a crash, the front-row fans flinch, BOOM +8 or +15, and the commentary calls it. A shattered panel lets\n  the puck out. At the next stoppage two glass techs skate out and put a new panel in (1.5 s, cosmetic).\n- **Accidental contact** knocks the referee or the mascot over too (comedy). Goalies can be knocked down only by a\n  KABOOM check (the crowd boos).\n- **Grudge** (per ordered pair, 0..100): +35 for being big-hit, +10 for being checked, +15 for being chirped, +10\n  when the rival big-hits a teammate. It decays 4/s after 3 s of peace.\n\n### 7.8 Deke and poke\n- **Deke** (`deke` with the puck): 0.45 s, a sideways cut of +90 toward the stick (alternating when the stick is\n  neutral), a spin animation (a spin-o-rama with turbo). Checks in its first 0.3 s miss with chance `0.7 + 0.04 (Hnd −\n  3)`. Cooldown 0.8 s. A goalie within 70 \"bites\" (7.6). A deke that leaves a defender behind within 1 s is a\n  `deke_beat` event (BOOM +6, commentary).\n- **Poke** (`deke` without the puck): 0.35 s, the blade reaches 18 ahead. If it passes within 8 of a carried puck,\n  steal chance is `T.pokeBase 0.55 + 0.08 (pokerHnd − carrierHnd)`. A miss leaves the poker off balance for 0.3 s.\n\n### 7.9 Chirping (`chirp`)\nPressing chirp makes the skater shout a line from `TEXT.chirps` at the nearest rival within 120: a speech bubble (2 s,\ntiny font, wrapped to 90 px) and babble in their voice. BOOM +3; the target's grudge +15; cooldown 4 s. CPU skaters\nchirp after big hits and goals (30%), and the human's chirps raise the chance that a CPU rival with Fight ≥ 4\nchallenges.\n\n### 7.10 The BOOM meter and KABOOM mode (`Boom`)\n- **One meter per team**, 0..100, × `T.boomGain` 1.0. Gains: big hit +18, check +6, glass crack +8 or shatter +15,\n  fight win +45, fight loss +5, goal +20, shot on goal +4, save (to the goalie's team) +5, completed pass +2,\n  one-timer +6, deke beat +6, chirp +3, BOOM Box item +40, mascot down +10, perfect Flood Wagon +30, Doris's organ\n  (chapter 5) +30.\n- **At 100 → KABOOM** for `T.kaboomTime` 15 s, or until the other team scores. A screen flash, an explosion burst over\n  the team's bench, \"KA-BOOM!\" (title font, shaking), the arena lights tint the team's color with a pulse, flame\n  cannons in the Dome, and the music's `kaboom` layer fades in (drums and distorted bass). For that team: infinite\n  turbo, the slapshot charges 2× faster, a full charge fires a **KABOOM shot**, checks are 2× strong, skates throw\n  sparks and leave molten `melt` trails, and their goalie reacts 0.03 s faster. The meter then resets to 0.\n- **KABOOM shot**: 760 u/s with zero error. The puck is a fireball (a glowing sprite, fire particles every step, a light\n  following it). Into the goalie → the blast (7.6). Into a skater → an explosion and a knockdown. Into the boards → an\n  explosion, and a hit panel shatters. A KABOOM goal: the net tips back in an explosion, a confetti and fire burst, a\n  double horn and fireworks in the Dome.\n- **Gilded Mode** is the Grizzlies' KABOOM (chapter 5): the same rules with gold flames.\n\n### 7.11 Fights and the sin bin (`Fight`)\n- **Trigger**: a human-controlled skater within 40 of a rival when either holds a grudge ≥ 40 against the other gets\n  the prompt `HOLD {lob} — DROP THE GLOVES`. Holding △ for 0.5 s challenges. A CPU rival accepts with\n  `clamp(0.4 + 0.12 (Fgt − 3) + grudge/200, 0.1, 0.95)` (forced in chapter 3 when the Bruise Brothers are involved).\n  A human rival (local or online) gets `HOLD {lob} TO ACCEPT` for 3 s. Declining is **turtling**: the decliner's team\n  BOOM −10 and the challenger's +10, and the crowd boos. A **CPU** with Fgt ≥ 4 and grudge ≥ 70 near a human-controlled\n  skater challenges them the same way. At most one fight per 60 s of clock and `T.fightMax` 3 per game.\n- **Staging**: a whistle; the clock stops; the camera moves to `brawler`, zoom 1.6, framing the two (`cam.frame`).\n  Gloves and helmets drop as sprites on the ice; the other skaters circle at 50; the referee and the linesman hover;\n  the crowd stands; the organ plays the fight vamp. The fight HUD shows two portraits with balance and stamina bars.\n- **Fighters**: balance 100 (`T.fightBalance`) and stamina 100 (regen 25/s); damage × `0.8 + 0.067 Fgt`.\n  - **Jab** (✕): 0.25 s, 6 damage, 8 stamina, staggers 0.12 s (rig: `jab`).\n  - **Haymaker** (□): wind-up 0.35 s (a clear telegraph: the arm draws back, a glint), active 0.1, recover 0.35. 18\n    damage (+6 if held up to 0.6 s), 22 stamina. A whiff leaves you open for 0.5 s (rig: `haymaker`, or `hook`\n    alternating).\n  - **Duck** (○): 0.35 s, immune to haymakers and half damage from jabs; 10 stamina; cooldown 0.4 (pose: `crouch` +\n    lean back).\n  - **Yank** (△): 0.3 s. If it lands, the rival's guard breaks for 0.6 s and they lose 15 stamina. **Three yanks\n    within 4 s pull the jersey over their head** (their rig gets `hood: true` in jersey color): blind for 1.5 s.\n  - With no stamina, everything is 40% slower.\n  - The CPU fighter ducks a haymaker wind-up with probability = its skill, and otherwise mixes jabs, haymakers and\n    yanks by personality.\n- **End**: balance ≤ 0 → that fighter falls (`down`); the winner raises a fist (`cheer`); a crowd roar; the winner's\n  team BOOM +45. The loser goes to the **sin bin** for `T.sinBin` 20 s of play clock (a \"POWER PLAY\" banner and timer\n  under the score bug), seated in the box, then steps out through the box door. If 20 s pass, the linesmen separate\n  them: a draw with no penalty and BOOM +10 each. Play resumes with a faceoff at the nearest dot.\n\n### 7.12 Fan throws, power-ups and hazards (`Items`)\n- **Throws**: every `T.itemEvery` 25–45 s of play, and 25% of the time right after a big hit or goal, a fan in the\n  stands throws (a lob arc from the crowd over the glass) onto the neutral or attacking zone. The item slides to a stop\n  and lasts 12 s (blinking for its last 3). Arena pools are in 11.2.\n- **Pickup**: a skater body within 12. Icons and timers show over the holder's head.\n\n| Item | Look | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| HOT SAUCE | red bottle (store `bottle`) | infinite turbo 8 s, fire trail |\n| GRANDMA'S TAPE | white tape roll | 10 s: can't lose the puck to pokes or checks below a big hit; passes can't be intercepted |\n| POUTINE | bowl of fries (store `bowl`) | 10 s: can't be knocked down; every check is a big hit (×1.6) |\n| LUMBER | a stick with a lightning bolt | the next 3 shots: +30% speed, zero error |\n| BRICK PADS | a brick | the holder's goalie grows ×1.35 for 12 s |\n| BOOM BOX | a boombox | +40 team BOOM |\n| HOT COCOA (pond only) | a steaming thermos | turbo refilled + 20% speed 8 s |\n\n| Hazard | Where | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| OCTOPUS | Grindhouse, Dome, cheat | a slip patch r 10: skaters crossing it `slip` (1.2 s, legs up, a slide); at the next stoppage the referee picks it up and twirls it overhead |\n| RUBBER RAT | Grindhouse | scurries randomly for 10 s; trips skaters (as slip) |\n| HATS | after any hat trick | 20–40 hats rain from the stands (cosmetic, swept up at the stoppage) |\n\n- **AI item greed**: a CPU skater not involved in the play (not the carrier, its marker or the pressure player)\n  detours to an item within 120 (`T.aiItemGreed`).\n- **Arena hazards**:\n  - **Thin ice** (pond): 3 elliptical patches (40 × 24) at fixed spots outside the creases, each with integrity 100.\n    A knockdown on a patch costs 50 and a big hit there 100. At 0 the patch breaks into a hole: black water, ripples\n    and a splash. A skater who enters a hole is `frozen` for 3 s (rig tinted icy blue inside a translucent block),\n    then pops out at the edge. A puck that falls in is lost, then a faceoff. Holes refreeze (as a darker patch) after\n    30 s or at intermission.\n  - **Snowbanks** (pond): the boards are snowbanks with no glass. Restitution .3 and a snow puff. A big hit into one\n    leaves the target `buried` for 1.5 s with only the head and skates showing.\n  - **Polar Pete** (mall): the mascot skates figure eights in the neutral zone during play. A moving obstacle (mass\n    1.5) that can be checked (\"MASCOT DOWN!\", BOOM +10); it gets up after 3 s and waves.\n  - **Discount Drop** (mall): every 40 s a ceiling claw lowers a crate to center ice; it breaks into a power-up.\n\n### 7.13 Team AI (`AI`)\n- **Cadence**: each CPU skater re-thinks every `lerp(0.3, 0.12, skill)` s and reacts after `lerp(0.35, 0.1, skill)`\n  s; between decisions it steers. Steering: seek the target, stay 12 from the boards unless chasing the puck, keep 40\n  from teammates, and avoid rivals while carrying.\n- **With the puck** (offense):\n  - **Carrier**: shoot when in the shooting zone (within 200 of the net, within ±60° of its axis, at most one body in the\n    lane), or when a one-timer pass is on. Pass when pressured (a rival within 26 ahead) or when a teammate is clearly\n    better placed (open lane, at least 60 closer to the net). Deke when a defender is square in front within 30 (40%\n    × Hnd/3). Otherwise carry toward the net, slaloming around defenders, with turbo in open ice.\n  - **Support forward**: get open on the far side at the dot height (about 150 from the goal line); once the carrier\n    crosses the blue line, drift to the far post or the slot for a one-timer.\n  - **Point**: stay at the blue line as an outlet; crash the net for rebounds when aggression is high.\n- **Without the puck** (defense):\n  - **Pressure**: the nearest skater intercepts the carrier's position 0.3 s ahead, then checks (when Hit ≥ 3 and\n    `RNG.sim() < aggression`) or pokes.\n  - **Cover**: marks the most dangerous rival without the puck (in the passing lane, or between them and the net).\n  - **Home**: guards the slot between the puck and its own net.\n- **Loose puck**: each team sends the skater who can reach the predicted puck position first. The rest take offense or\n  defense spots according to which team will probably win the race.\n- **Faceoffs**: centers face off at the dot; wingers line up on both sides; the point man behind.\n- **Difficulty** (Settings): Rookie, Pro, All-Star, Legend set AI skill .35 / .55 / .75 / .95, CPU goalie reaction\n  offsets +.06 / +.02 / 0 / −.02 s, and the human team's goalie −.03 / −.01 / 0 / +.01. Light rubber-banding (CPU\n  skill −.1 while it leads by 3 or more) on Rookie only.\n- **Teammates of humans** use the same AI and also obey call-for-pass. Team tactics from story choices: **Finesse**\n  (pass bias +30%, speed +4%) or **Grit** (check bias +30%, BOOM gain +15%).\n\n### 7.14 Match flow (`Match`)\n- **Configuration**: `{ home, away, arena, periods: 3, periodLen: 120, ot: 'sudden' (120 s, 3-on-3) | 'none',\n  shootout: true, intros: true, replays: 'auto', flood: 'ask' | 'always' | 'never', difficulty, cheats, objectives,\n  script, humans: [{ team, input }] }`.\n- **Phases**: `intro` → `faceoff` → `play` ⇄ `stoppage` → `goal` → `replay` → `faceoff` … `periodEnd` →\n  `intermission` (Flood Wagon) → `faceoff` … `final` → `results`. Also `fight`, `ot`, `shootout` and `celebration`.\n  The clock counts down only in `play`. The engine's pause freezes everything.\n- **Faceoff**: the referee holds the puck, raises an arm and drops it after a random 0.6–1.2 s. Each center presses\n  `pass` or `shoot` when it drops; the earlier press within 0–0.25 s after the drop wins (a press before the drop is a\n  slow, mistimed swipe); a CPU center reacts after its skill delay. The winner's swipe sends the puck back to a\n  teammate.\n- **Stoppages**: a frozen puck, the puck out of play, after a fight, at the end of a sin-bin call. Each brings a\n  whistle, a 1.5 s pause, a lower-third stat card (shots, hits, faceoffs %), an organ sting, and then the faceoff.\n- **Goals**: the horn (3 s), the red goal light spinning behind that net, the team's goal song sting, the crowd jumping,\n  the scorer's celebration (chosen by personality: fist pump, sniper aim, knee slide, stick guitar, a bounce off the\n  glass), and teammates converging. \"GOAL!\" in the title font, the scoring summary (scorer and assists, the\n  last two touches by the scorer's team), then an **instant replay** (7.16), then a center faceoff.\n- **Hat trick**: a player's third goal makes hats rain, and the commentary calls it. **Hoser Hat Trick**: one player\n  with a goal, an assist and a fight win in one game, shown as a toast.\n- **Periods**: the buzzer at 0:00, then the period summary card. **Intermission**: the Flood Wagon minigame (offered\n  per the `flood` option; skipping runs a 6 s AI resurfacing fast-forward), then the next period. Teams switch ends\n  every period.\n- **Overtime**: sudden death; a tie after it goes to the shootout (exhibition and story). In session mode: at most 60\n  s of sudden death, then a tie.\n- **Shootout**: 3 rounds each (home first), then sudden-death rounds. A shooter starts at center with the puck and an\n  8-second shot clock; the attempt ends on a shot, a save, a goal, or the puck going backward. Humans shoot for their\n  team (the skaters rotate) and play goalie against the CPU's shooters (6.1). The HUD shows big ✓ and ✗ marks.\n- **Final**: the final horn, the winning team celebrates, the losers slump (`kneel`), then **results**.\n- **Stats** per skater: goals, assists, shots, hits, big hits, takeaways, fights won, turbo used, top shot speed.\n  Per goalie: saves and shots against. Per team: everything summed, plus BOOM filled and Kabooms.\n- **Three stars**: rank players by `3 G + 2 A + 0.5 bigHits + 1.5 fightsWon + 0.3 shots` (goalies:\n  `0.12 saves + 2 × (save% − .85) × 10`) and announce the third, second and first stars, each with a portrait card and a\n  commentary line.\n- **Objectives**: declarative `{ id, text, on: 'goal' | 'hit' | …, where(e, match) }` counters plus a `need`, checked\n  live. A star toast when one is met.\n\n### 7.15 Camera director (`Cam`)\n- **Play**: focus on the puck (or carrier) plus a lead of 0.25 s of puck velocity. If a lone human's skater is more\n  than 220 from the puck, shift 25% toward them. With several local humans, `cam.frame([puck, ...humans],\n  { margin: 60, zoom: [.78, 1] })`. `cam.smooth` .15; bounds from `map.bounds(view)`.\n- **Zoom**: 1.0 (Settings → Camera distance: Near 1.15, Normal 1.0, Far 0.85); 1.15 at faceoffs; a 1.1 punch on big\n  hits (0.3 s); out to 0.85 briefly when the puck flies faster than 400.\n- **Fights**: `brawler`, zoom 1.6, framing the fighters. **Celebrations**: 1.3 on the scorer. **Intros**: a dolly\n  along the lineup. **Replays**: 7.16. Then back to the player's camera setting (Broadcast `threequarter` or Overhead\n  `topdown`, cycled by the `camera` action and saved).\n\n### 7.16 Instant replay (`Replay`)\n- **Recorder**: every second step, push `{ puck, skaters and goalies: { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, rigState }, events }`\n  into an 8 s ring buffer. `rigState` is the object passed to `rig.update`, so the replay re-poses rigs exactly.\n- **Goal replay**: once the celebration has played for 1.5 s, cut (a puck-shaped wipe) to the last 4 s before the goal\n  at 0.5× in the `brawler` view following the puck at zoom 1.25, with letterbox bars, a \"REPLAY\" bug, and the\n  recorded events re-firing their effects. ✕ (or confirm) skips. Setting: Replays Auto or Off. Big-hit and Kaboom\n  replays (3 s) also play at the next stoppage when Replays is Auto: when such an event happens, copy its clip (2 s\n  before to 1 s after) out of the ring buffer, because the buffer will have moved on by the stoppage.\n- **Highlights**: keep the 3 best clips of a story run (goal type and hit power score them) in memory for the end\n  credits.\n\n### 7.17 Commentary (`Talk`)\n- **Booth**: CHUCK WALLOP (play-by-play) and MOOSE PLUNKETT (color), with live portraits (rigs in suits) in a bottom\n  subtitle box. Two lines at most; non-modal, auto-advancing (`talk.say(text, { modal: false, auto: 2.4, portrait,\n  name })`).\n- **Selection**: each event type has a pool (`TEXT.talk[type]`) with priority and cooldowns: a global 1.2 s, the\n  same line 120 s, the same type 6 s. Goals, fights, Kabooms and glass breaks interrupt; filler (Moose's anecdotes)\n  only plays after 8 s of quiet play. Variables: `{name} {team} {victim} {goalie} {score} {arena} {period}`.\n- **Voices**: every line babbles (10.1) in the speaker's voice. Settings: Commentary On/Off, Subtitles On/Off,\n  Voices volume.\n- **Tips** (Coach Marge) are separate: a banner just below the score bug with glyph chips, shown the first time its\n  trigger fires per save profile (Appendix D).\n\n### 7.18 HUD (`Hud`; it keeps clear of `game.cornerArea()` and inside a 92% title-safe area)\n- **Score bug** (top center, about 200 × 30): team logo chips, abbreviations, scores at font scale 2, the period\n  (`1ST 2ND 3RD OT SO`), the clock `m:ss`, and under each team its BOOM meter (80 × 4; flames and a countdown while in\n  KABOOM).\n- **Power play** strip under it: `POWER PLAY MUK 0:14`, with the sin-binned player's tag.\n- **Player markers**: a colored ring decal under each human's skater (P1–P4 in `E.PLAYER_COLORS`, the seat colors\n  online), a chevron with `P1` above, and an arrow on the screen edge when they are off screen. A turbo bar (16 × 2)\n  under the chevron. The shot meter above the shooter while charging (gold when full).\n- **Radar** (bottom right, about 108 × 48): the rink outline, skaters as team-colored dots, humans as larger dots with\n  rings, the puck white.\n- **Prompts** (bottom center, above the subtitles): context chips (`{shoot} ONE-TIMER!`, `HOLD {lob} DROP THE GLOVES`,\n  `{pass} SKIP`).\n- **Banners**: GOAL!, SAVE!, POST!, BIG HIT!, THROUGH THE GLASS!, KA-BOOM!, FIGHT!, POWER PLAY, HAT TRICK!, PERIOD\n  2, FINAL, in the title font with shake and color cycling (honoring reduce motion).\n- **Fight HUD**: two portraits with bars at the top corners, and the fight control chips at the bottom.\n- **Lower-thirds** at stoppages: one broadcast-style stat card for 3 s.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Art direction\n\n**Base**: the engine's native look (`res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`, HD Humanoids at size 1.2–1.3, lit scenes, shaded with\n`E.tones`, props, particles), aimed at Symphony of the Night and Metal Slug quality, as AI_GUIDE asks. Act on every\nlook note from `tools/check.mjs`.\n\n- **Skaters**: build `heroic` at size 1.2 (enforcers `bulky` at 1.3). Long-sleeved jersey (`outfit: 'shirt'`,\n  `sleeves: 'long'`, `colors.cloth` the jersey, `trim` the stripe), breezers in `pants`, socks in the team color, skates,\n  big gloves (`glove`), a hockey helmet, number and letter, `weapon: 'stick'`, and shoulder pads (`armor: true`, plate\n  in the jersey color). Hair shows under the helmet (some flow, mullets on the Lumberjacks). Beards come from a darker\n  skin tone on the jaw: add a `beard` color option if needed and log it.\n- **Goalies**: `bulky` at 1.3 (The Vault 1.75), pads, blocker, catcher, mask, `gstick`, and pad and mask colors per\n  team.\n- **Referees**: `heroic` at 1.15, white shirt with black stripes, orange armbands (`trim`), a black helmet, a whistle\n  (one dot).\n- **Crowd**: as in the SPORTS kit: two small fans per stand tile (4 × 5 shirt, 3 × 3 head), colored 70% home and 30%\n  away, swaying. Excitement drives them: claps, standing, jumping on goals, hands on heads after a big hit, a wave\n  around the arena when quiet for 20 s. Fans hold signs (tiny-font text: `BARN BURNER`, `KABOOM!`, `MARGE 4 PM`,\n  `SAVE THE ICEBOX`, `PIPESY ♥`). Behind each net, 4–6 bigger **glass pounders** (Humanoid at size 0.9 in the classic\n  style) bang the glass when play comes near. On the near side, a row of dark head-and-shoulder silhouettes is drawn\n  in screen space along the bottom edge when the camera is low (the broadcast foreground).\n- **Team logos**: a 24 × 24 string sprite each (`E.sprite` rows plus a palette of 4–6 colors), used at center ice (×3),\n  in the score bug (scaled down to 12 or 16), on menu cards (×3) and on bench banners. Section 11.1 describes them.\n- **Effects**: ice spray on stops and turns (white `dust` and `bits`); a skate shower when someone is hit; glass shards;\n  a puck streak; a slapshot shockwave ring; KABOOM fire, explosions and sparks; steam from melt; snow (weather) at the\n  pond; confetti; hats; an octopus splat; a flying tooth on a big fight punch (a white bit, \"chiclets\"); dizzy stars\n  circling a knocked-down head; sweat drops in fights; turbo speed lines.\n- **Lighting**: canvas lights in every arena (11.2 lists them). Goal lights pulse red behind the net. KABOOM tints the\n  arena. Spotlights sweep during intros and the title.\n- **UI style**: dark blue-black panels (`E.ui.box` gradients) with ice-white text and a gold accent (`#ffd36a`),\n  with team colors on cards. Theme the engine's HTML screens with `new E.Shell(game, { theme })` in the same colors and\n  a large font: body text at least 24 CSS px at 1080p (check a screenshot).\n\n---\n\n## 9. Animation (the engine's procedural rigs plus new hockey motion)\n\nHockey motion is added by **wrapping `rig.solvePose`** on each skater and goalie rig (`Rigs`). It overrides feet,\nknees, hips, torso lean, hands and stick joints (`E.ik3` for knees and elbows) from a small state the Skater passes\nin (`skate: { phase, push, lean, stop, back, cross }`, `stick: { blade: [f, s, z], top, follow }`). Fights, cheers and\nfalls use the engine's own `attack` moves, `pose`, `down` and `flip`. Every animation below must play in all three views.\n\n| Motion | How |\n|---|---|\n| Skating stride | Phase advances by `speed / 22`. Each foot pushes back and out diagonally (3 o'clock or 9 o'clock), then recovers under the hip. Knees bend 35°, hips drop 2.5, the torso leans .35 rad (.5 with turbo). The free arm swings when not stick-handling |\n| Glide | Feet parallel, knees soft, a slight sway |\n| Crossovers | Turning hard at speed: the outside foot crosses over in front, alternating |\n| Hockey stop | The torso turns 70° off the velocity, both blades skid sideways with a deep knee bend, a spray at the feet |\n| Backward C-cuts | The hips swing, the feet trace C shapes (AI defenders only) |\n| Stick-handling | The blade weaves ±3 in front; the hands follow (the top hand at the hip, the bottom hand 40% down the shaft) |\n| Pass / saucer | The blade sweeps back to front toward the target; a saucer flicks up at the end |\n| Wrist shot | Weight shift, a fast sweep, a high follow-through |\n| Slapshot | Wind-up (the stick rises behind the shoulder and holds while charging), downswing to the ice, follow-through pointing at the target |\n| One-timer | A short wind-up already held, then the strike on contact |\n| Deke | Spin-o-rama (a 360° body spin with `flip`-like twist), toe drag (the blade pulls the puck back across) |\n| Check | The shoulder leads (lean into it), the stick across the chest |\n| Hit reaction / fall | A stagger (bump); `down` + `flip` tumble + a belly slide (big hit); squashed against the glass (`rig.kick(-.4)`) when hit into it; `getup` from a kneel |\n| Poke | The stick shoots forward along the ice in a lunge |\n| Slip | Feet fly up, landing on the back, a spin-slide (octopus, rat) |\n| Goalie | A ready crouch (pads together, glove up), shuffle and T-push, butterfly (knees down, pads flared), glove and blocker saves, pad stack, poke, covering the puck, celebrating, blasted (flailing backward into the net) |\n| Faceoff | Centers crouch with sticks down; the referee raises an arm and drops the puck; the swipe |\n| Celebrations | Fist pump, sniper aim (the stick held like a rifle), knee slide, stick guitar, bouncing off the glass, a team huddle |\n| Fights | Gloves off (sprites fall), circling in `stance: 'guard'`, one hand gripping the rival's jersey (the hand held at the rival's shoulder), `jab`, `haymaker` and `hook` from `E.MOVES`, a duck, jersey over the head (`hood`), the knockdown, the winner's `cheer` |\n| Bench and coach | Spares sit (a sit pose via solvePose: hips at bench height, knees forward); Coach Marge gestures (`wave`, `hips`) |\n| Story set pieces | The handshake line (two lines sliding past, hands out), the Cup lift (`cheer` with the Cup sprite held at the hands), the Flood Wagon driver seated and steering, Polar Pete's dance (a bulky white rig, a big round head from an extra ball drawn over it, ears), the organist playing (hands bobbing on the beat via `audio.onBeat`) |\n\n**Animation lab** (`#lab`, also in the Dev panel): one skater, one goalie and one referee on a small rink, a list of\nevery motion above, a slider for speed and phase, and a `brawler` / `threequarter` / `topdown` toggle. Film each\nmotion with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` (`--seed 1`) and check: the wind-up, the strike, the settle, no snaps or backward\nsweeps.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Audio (all synthesized in code; no audio files)\n\n### 10.1 Voices: babble (Animalese/Simlish style)\n- `Synth.babble(text, voice, { onLetter })` turns a line into syllables. Each letter that sounds (vowels, and\n  consonants as onsets) is a 55–85 ms blip: a `pulse` or `saw` source through two bandpass filters at the vowel's\n  formants (a: 800/1200 Hz, e: 500/1900, i: 300/2300, o: 500/900, u: 350/700; consonants borrow the next vowel and add\n  a 10 ms noise click for `s t k p` sounds). Pitch is the voice's base × (a letter-hash offset of ±3 semitones). `!`\n  raises the last 4 syllables by 4 semitones; `?` glides the last syllable up; `,` and `.` add 120 / 220 ms pauses.\n  It runs on the engine's new `voice` bus.\n- A voice is `{ base: Hz, range: semitones, speed: syllables/s, wave, formantShift, gruff (noise mix) }`. Marge: low,\n  gruff, slow. Dunny: mid and bright. Snipes: high and fast. Lou: very low, soft and slow. Lemmy: mid and wobbly\n  (vibrato). Glitterman: nasal (formants × 1.15), fast. Chuck: mid-high, very fast. Moose: low and gruff. The referee\n  barks single syllables. The crowd's chant mixes 6 voices.\n- It hooks into `E.Dialog` through the voice hook (section 4) for cutscenes and the booth, and into chirp bubbles,\n  intros (\"Number NINE… DUNNY… MACPHAIL!\"), the referee's calls and crowd chants. Its randomness comes from `RNG.fx`\n  so it never changes the simulation.\n\n### 10.2 Sound effects (`audio.define` voices; custom graphs where noted)\nSkate stride swish (filtered noise, pitch by speed, one per push); hockey stop \"shhhk\" (noise, a bandpass sweep down);\npuck on stick \"tock\"; pass \"thwap\"; wrist shot \"snap\"; slapshot crack plus whoosh; one-timer (a louder crack); **post\n\"PING\"** (triangle 1850 Hz, 0.9 s decay, a slight detune: the most recognizable sound in hockey); crossbar ping (2100\nHz); puck on boards (a low thud and a rattle); puck on glass (a sharp clack and a ring); net swish; body check thump\nplus a babble \"oof\"; big hit (a deeper thump, a glass rattle, crowd \"OHHH\"); glass crack (a sharp tick) and glass\nshatter (a noise burst and a descending sine tinkle cluster of 12 voices); the referee's whistle (a two-tone pea\nwhistle with vibrato); **the goal horn** (a custom graph: 3 detuned `brass` oscillators at 98, 147 and 196 Hz through\nthe lowpass `lp: 900`, 0.25 s attack, 2.6 s hold, then release, plus noise \"air\"); the period buzzer (square at 220 Hz,\n1.5 s); punches (a thud and a whoosh); dizzy stars twinkle; power-up pickup (an arpeggio); item throw (a whoosh);\noctopus \"splort\"; KABOOM explosion (engine `explode` + a sub-bass drop); the Flood Wagon engine (a looped low saw\nputter, pitch by speed), its horn \"A-OOGA\"; menu move, select and back (soft organ blips).\n\n### 10.3 Crowd and organ\n- **Crowd bed**: two looped noise sources (bandpass 400 Hz and 1.2 kHz, an LFO swell) whose gain follows\n  `Crowd.excitement` (0..1: raised by shots, near misses, hits, goals; decays). Plus reactions: \"OHHH\" (a swell\n  sweeping down), \"AHHH\" (a near miss), cheer (a burst with high-voiced babble), boo (low, filtered babble), the\n  \"KA-BOOM!\" chant (6-voice babble on the beat, with claps), and claps in rhythm.\n- **The organ** (`organ` wave, a Leslie-like vibrato of 6 Hz at .004): original stings only. A rising charge fanfare\n  (G4 C5 E5 G5 – E5 G5), a chromatic walk-up vamp for faceoffs, a clap-along vamp (\"da-da-da da-da\"), a sad trombone\n  slide for an opponent's penalty, a fight vamp (minor and tense), and a goal sting per team. In the Ol' Icebox, Doris\n  the organist plays them visibly. **Never copy existing chants or songs** (no \"Charge!\" bugle call, no stadium rock\n  standards).\n\n### 10.4 Music (engine song format; the new `organ` and `brass` waves; named layers)\n| Song | Use | Character |\n|---|---|---|\n| `theme` | title, attract | arena chip-rock anthem: saw power chords, a driving square lead, drums; the \"Ice Hoc-Kaboom\" hook |\n| `menu` | menus, setup | a relaxed loop from the theme's chords |\n| `locker` | cutscenes (locker room) | gritty bass and a snare shuffle, organ pads |\n| `pond` | pond cutscenes, the pond arena's stoppages | a folksy pulse-wave fiddle tune in 6/8 |\n| `grind` | Grindhouse | a punk loop |\n| `mall` | MegaMall | cheesy synth-pop |\n| `final` | Dome cutscenes, the final | epic, brass |\n| `play` | under play (quiet) | a low pulse plus layers `drive` (in the third period and OT), `kaboom` (KABOOM mode), `fight` (fights) |\n| `flood` | the Flood Wagon minigame | an original skaters' waltz (3/4, organ) |\n| `victory`, `defeat` | results | a fanfare, a sad trombone |\n| `credits` | the end credits | the theme as a ballad, then full band |\n| goal stings ×6 | one per team | 2 bars over the horn |\n\n**Mix**: buses `music` (setting), `sfx` (setting), `voice` (setting: Voices) and the crowd (on sfx, plus its own\nsetting: Crowd). Duck the music under the commentary voice (−4 dB) and in the pause menu (the engine does this).\n\n---\n\n## 11. Content\n\n### 11.1 Teams (3 skaters + 1 goalie each; ratings 1–5: Spd / Sht / Pas / Hit / Fgt / Hnd; goalies Rfx / Size / Reb)\n| Team | Abbr | Home dark / away white trim | Logo (24×24) | Players |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Mukluk Falls Muskrats** | MUK | brown `#5a3a22`, gold `#e8b43a`, cream `#f3e6c8` | a buck-toothed muskrat face in a gold ring | #9 Duncan \"Dunny\" MacPhail, C, playmaker 4/3/5/3/2/4, shoots L · #19 Priya \"Snipes\" Sandhu, sniper 5/5/3/2/2/5, R · #44 Lou \"Big Lou\" Beaudoin, enforcer D (bulky) 2/4/2/5/5/2, R · G #31 Lemmy \"The Sieve\" Kowalchuk 3/4/3 (trait: **Talks to Posts**: 20% of goals within 4 of a post ring off it instead) |\n| **Dryfork Drillers** | DRY | black `#1d1d22`, orange `#f07a1a` | an oil derrick with a drop | #7 \"Rig\" McCoy, C 3/3/4/3/3/3 · #15 \"Gusher\" Gomez 4/4/3/2/2/4 · #2 \"Drill Bit\" Dobbs, D 3/2/2/4/3/2 · G #35 Derrick Okafor 2/3/2 |\n| **Logjam Lumberjacks** | LOG | red plaid `#b3262a` + black, cream | a bearded log face | #10 Axel Sundqvist, C 3/4/3/3/3/3 · #27 \"Sawdust\" Sally Lindgren 4/4/3/3/2/4 · #88 \"Big Timber\" Thibodeau, enforcer (bulky) 2/3/2/5/4/2 · G #1 \"Stumpy\" O'Rourke 3/4/3 |\n| **Grindhouse Bruise Brothers** | GRD | purple `#4b2a6b`, lime `#9be04a` | a fist inside a gear | #66 Rocco Bruiser (bulky) 3/3/2/5/5/2 · #67 Rollo Bruiser (bulky) 3/3/2/5/5/2 · #12 \"Mumbles\" Malone 4/4/3/2/3/4 · G #29 \"Tank\" Tankersley 3/5/2 |\n| **Megaplex Marauders** | MEG | teal `#18b5b0`, magenta `#e0389a` | a shopping cart flying a pirate flag | #23 Chad Glitterman, C 4/3/4/2/1/4 · #8 \"Zoom\" Zhang 5/3/3/2/2/4 · #5 \"Promo\" Perkins, D 3/3/3/4/3/3 · G #40 \"Kiosk\" Kingsley 4/3/4 |\n| **Gilded Grizzlies** | GLD | gold `#d9a520`, black `#141414`, white | a grizzly head in a crown | #1 Sterling Glitterman Jr. 5/5/4/3/2/5 (**Golden Twister**) · #91 \"Silk\" Sullivan 4/3/5/2/2/5 · #55 \"Brick\" Brickowski (bulky) 3/4/2/5/5/2 · G #00 **The Vault** 5/5/5 (boss: size 1.75) |\n\n- **Rating multipliers**: speed `0.85 + 0.05 Spd`; shot speed `0.85 + 0.05 Sht`, shot error `1.3 − 0.1 Sht`; pass\n  speed `0.9 + 0.033 Pas`; check `0.8 + 0.067 Hit`; fight damage `0.8 + 0.067 Fgt`; pickup radius `0.85 + 0.05 Hnd`.\n  Goalie reaction `−0.015 (Rfx − 3)`, save shapes × `0.9 + 0.033 Size`, freeze chance `+0.06 (Reb − 3)`.\n- **Golden Twister** (Sterling): in the offensive zone, 1 in 3 carries end in a 0.6 s spin with a golden glow\n  (telegraphed), then a curving shot (spin 1.2, like the SPORTS kit's curl) that cuts the CPU goalie's save chance by\n  25%. Checking him during the spin is a guaranteed big hit and BOOM +10.\n- **The Vault**: size 1.75; the first two KABOOM shots only stagger him (\"VAULT LOCKED\"). After the second, \"THE\n  VAULT IS CRACKED!\": size 1.4 and Rfx −1 for the rest of the game. Weak to cross-crease one-timers (lateral speed ×\n  0.8) and dekes (he bites 1.5×).\n- **Coach and staff portraits**: Coach Marge Pelletier (grey bun, cardigan, whistle), Old Gus (90, cap, the Flood\n  Wagon driver), Doris (organist, beehive hair), Goldie Glitterman (gold fur coat, sunglasses), Polar Pete (mascot),\n  and Chuck and Moose (suits; Moose is missing teeth).\n\n### 11.2 Arenas\n| Arena | Chapter | Look | Lights | Items | Hazard | Music |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **The Ol' Icebox** (Mukluk Falls) | 1, title, practice | wooden barrel-vault beams, string lights, 1962 championship banners, wooden stands, fans in toques, Doris's organ booth, a hand-painted scoreboard, ads (`MUKLUK MUFFLER & TIRE`, `KOWALCHUK'S PEROGIES`, `BAIT 'N' BAGELS`) | ambient .65 warm, 6 hanging lamps over the ice (light radius 260) | Hot Sauce, Tape, Poutine, BOOM Box | – | organ, `play` |\n| **Lake Kabonk** (pond) | 2 | a frozen lake at dusk, snowbank boards, pines, two cabins with lit windows, a bonfire with fans in parkas, string lights on poles, snowmen (store) | ambient .45 blue dusk, bonfire flicker, cabin windows, string lights; weather snow .5 | Hot Cocoa, Tape, Lumber, BOOM Box | thin ice ×3, snowbanks | `pond` |\n| **The Grindhouse** | 3 | a steel-truss mill arena, chain-link above the end boards, steam pipes, rowdy stands, a cage-match vibe, ads (`RUSTBELT SCRAP`, `IRON GUT CHILI`) | ambient .5 cool green, flickering fluorescents (`RNG.fx`), steam vents | Poutine, Lumber, BOOM Box | octopus throws after goals, rubber rats | `grind` |\n| **MegaMall Ice Palace** | 4 | a rink in a mall atrium: storefront neon, escalators, a fountain, a food court, ads on every inch (`GLITTERMAN MEGAPLEX — COMING SOON!`) | ambient .7, neon emissives in magenta and teal, fountain glow | Discount Drop crates (any item) | Polar Pete, Discount Drop | `mall` |\n| **The Kaboom Dome** | 5 | a huge arena: gold-trimmed boards, flame cannons in the corners, laser lights, fireworks, a sold-out crowd, a jumbotron frame on replays | ambient .55, strong white ceiling lights, moving spotlights in intros, flame light on goals and Kabooms | Hot Sauce, Brick Pads, BOOM Box | octopus (rare), Gilded Mode | `final` |\n\nEvery arena uses the same rink geometry. Walls, stands and props come from the TileMap (`types` for tiers with `face`\nmaterials), `r.shape` / `E.SHAPES` (new entries: `locker`, `bench-box`, `organ`, `net`, `glass-crew-cart`,\n`flood-wagon`, `flame-cannon`, `cabin`, `fountain`, `escalator`, `storefront`, `scoreboard`, `kaboom-cup`) and\n`r.prop` (lamps, banners, signs, torches as bonfire, trees).\n\n### 11.3 Story: THE CUP RUN\n\n**Premise**: Mukluk Falls (pop. 812) has one thing: the Ol' Icebox, a 1950s barn where the town learned to skate.\nDeveloper Goldie Glitterman bought the land and plans a \"Megaplex Parking Experience\". Coach Marge digs up **Town\nBylaw 1897-B**: *any rink that houses the Kaboom Cup shall stand forever.* So the Muskrats, a ragtag team of three\nskaters, a superstitious goalie and a 72-year-old coach, have to win the regional Kaboom Cup: five games, five\nbarns, five rivals. **Tone**: a small-town sports-movie comedy told like a hockey broadcast, with hockey clichés","numLines":500,"startLine":400,"totalLines":1473}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XxGm4zCJEh3XtHbK7ckCvF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
