{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvBtCwVkyXnWnpDk11V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ux91F44i72kLjmKDpPDt32","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-055058__x9a2bbb/work/PLAN.md","offset":900,"limit":450},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21501,"cache_read_input_tokens":38232,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21501},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de63938e-b4cc-4b63-8e8c-4cc91a6c7b2f","uuid":"7d487ace-9e3d-4961-af4e-1bfb4c2367de","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:51:11.591Z","request_id":"req_011CghvBsodZYmDmbLccSZ5j","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Ux91F44i72kLjmKDpPDt32":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-055058__x9a2bbb/work/PLAN.md","offset":900,"limit":450}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ux91F44i72kLjmKDpPDt32","type":"tool_result","content":"900\tplayed with a straight face, chirps that rhyme, and big heart. PG: no blood, no slurs, no swearing (a beep and\n901\tbabble stand in for \"a curse word\").\n902\t\n903\t**Chapter flow**: storymap (a snowy highway map; the team bus drives between 5 town stops, each showing its stars and\n904\tlock) → pre-game cutscene (with one choice) → [chapter 1: optional warm-up drills 1–3] → player intros → the game (its\n905\tobjectives listed on the pause screen and a pre-game card) → intermission Flood Wagon (offered) → post-game cutscene →\n906\tresults and three stars → stars and unlocks → back to the map. **A loss**: a short Marge pep talk (a different one for\n907\teach chapter, in TEXT) and Retry or Back to Map. Progress autosaves (`game.saves`) after each chapter and choice.\n908\t\n909\t**Choices** (one per chapter; they set the game's team tactic, 7.13): chapter 1 \"Clean and fast\" (Finesse) / \"Mean and\n910\tloud\" (Grit); chapter 2 the same two; chapter 3 \"Let Lou loose\" (Lou Fgt +1, fights likelier) / \"Keep it on the ice\" (Lou\n911\tPas +1); chapter 4 \"Ignore the bear\" / \"Hunt the bear\" (the AI targets Polar Pete); chapter 5 \"Doris plays early\"\n912\t(the organ boost at the start of the 2nd period) / \"Doris plays late\" (at 5:00 left in the 3rd, +50% stronger).\n913\t\n914\t| # | Chapter | Arena / rival / rules | New mechanic spotlighted | Objectives (★ each) |\n915\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n916\t| 1 | **Home Opener** | Ol' Icebox vs Dryfork Drillers, 3 × 1:30; the rivals play one difficulty step below the setting (never below Rookie) | skating, passing, shooting, one-timers, checking, BOOM meter, Flood Wagon | Win · Score a one-timer · Land 3 big hits |\n917\t| 2 | **Pond Rules** | Lake Kabonk vs Logjam Lumberjacks, 3 × 1:30 | KABOOM mode (Marge explains it), power-ups, thin ice, snowbanks | Win · Break the ice under a Lumberjack · Trigger KABOOM |\n918\t| 3 | **Gloves Off** | Grindhouse vs Bruise Brothers, 3 × 1:30, they challenge often | fights, the sin bin, power plays, hazards (octopi, rats), chirps | Win · Win 2 fights · Score a power-play goal |\n919\t| 4 | **Mall Brawl** | MegaMall vs Megaplex Marauders, 3 × 1:30 with no OT, then a **Shootout Showcase** every time (it decides a tie; otherwise it is a bonus round for mall money and a toast) | the mascot, Discount Drop, the shootout and manual goalie | Win · Score a KABOOM goal · Knock down Polar Pete |\n920\t| 5 | **The Kaboom Cup** | Kaboom Dome vs Gilded Grizzlies, 3 × 2:00, OT and shootout if tied | the boss: Sterling's Golden Twister, The Vault, Gilded Mode, Glitterman's Gilded Boost (Grizzlies +10% speed from the 3rd period), Doris's organ counter (Muskrats BOOM +30 and +10% speed for 20 s) | Win · Beat The Vault with a deke goal · One player scores a hat trick |\n921\t\n922\t**Script beats** (TEXT holds the full lines; these set the voice. Speakers in caps, choices in brackets):\n923\t\n924\t*Chapter 1 pre-game (locker room)*\n925\t- MARGE: \"Sit down, shut up, and listen. I got a letter.\"\n926\t- MARGE: \"Goldie Glitterman bought the land under the Icebox. Wants to pave it for a {c=#ffd36a}Megaplex Parking\n927\t  Experience{/c}.\"\n928\t- DUNNY: \"A parking… experience? Beauty. Wait. No. Not beauty.\"\n929\t- SNIPES: \"This barn's got more character than his whole bank account. And his haircut.\"\n930\t- MARGE: \"Bylaw 1897-B. Any rink that houses the Kaboom Cup stands forever. So we win the Cup.\"\n931\t- LOU (knitting): \"Five games, then. Like the five petals of the wild rose.\"\n932\t- LEMMY: \"Pipesy says we win. Clang's not so sure. Clang's a pessimist.\"\n933\t- GLITTERMAN (in the doorway): \"Enjoy the barn, folks. I've ordered the parking meters. Gold ones.\"\n934\t- MARGE: \"Captain. Tell 'em how we play tonight.\" [CLEAN AND FAST / MEAN AND LOUD]\n935\t- DUNNY: \"We get pucks deep, we get bodies to the net, and we— uh— {$tacticLine}\"\n936\t- MARGE: \"Warm-up's on. Then we drill the Drillers.\"\n937\t\n938\t*Chapter 1 post-game*: CHUCK: \"The Muskrats take the opener! The Icebox is ROCKIN'!\" · GLITTERMAN: \"Beginner's luck.\n939\tThe meters are still on order.\" · MARGE: \"Pack your long johns. Lake Kabonk. Pond rules.\"\n940\t\n941\t*Chapter 2 pre-game (the lake at dusk, by the bonfire)*: BIG TIMBER: \"Welcome to the woods, Muskrats. We don't check.\n942\tWe FELL.\" · SNIPES: \"Cute beard. Did you grow it, or did a beaver move in?\" · LEMMY: \"The ice is talking. It says\n943\t'crack'.\" · MARGE: \"Thin ice is a tool. Hit 'em where it's thin.\" · MARGE: \"And listen. When the whole team's hummin'\n944\t— hits, passes, the crowd losin' its mind — the ice starts to shake. That's a KABOOM. Fill the meter and let it\n945\trip.\" · LOU: \"Like thunder in a teacup.\" · [tactic choice]\n946\t*Post*: BIG TIMBER: \"You hit like a falling spruce. Good on ya.\" · DUNNY: \"Thanks! You smell like one!\" · MARGE: \"Next\n947\tstop, the Grindhouse. Bring a mouthguard. Bring two.\"\n948\t\n949\t*Chapter 3 pre-game (the Grindhouse's dim locker room)*: ROCCO: \"Well, well. Lou Beaudoin.\" · ROLLO: \"Lou 'The\n950\tLibrary' Beaudoin.\" · ROCCO: \"Heard you knit now.\" · ROLLO: \"Heard you purl.\" · LOU: \"I have retired from fisticuffs,\n951\tgentlemen.\" · MARGE: \"Retire after the game.\" · MARGE: \"In this barn they drop the gloves, you drop 'em back. Win the\n952\tscrap, win the barn. Lose it, you sit in the sin bin and think about your choices.\" · [LET LOU LOOSE / KEEP IT ON THE\n953\tICE]\n954\t*Post*: ROLLO: \"He knitted me a scarf.\" · ROCCO: \"For my neck.\" · ROLLO: \"Which he bruised.\" · LOU: \"There is an ice pack\n955\tin the pocket.\" · MARGE: \"Next, the Megaplex. Glitterman's turf. Watch your wallets.\"\n956\t\n957\t*Chapter 4 pre-game (rink-side under the neon)*: CHAD (filming himself): \"What's up, Mall Rats! Smash that glass,\n958\tbro!\" · DUNNY: \"We're Muskrats.\" · CHAD: \"Same content, bro.\" · GLITTERMAN (to Lemmy): \"Name your price, goalie.\" ·\n959\tLEMMY: \"…Pipesy says no. Clang says no with a curse word.\" · POLAR PETE: (a dance and a muffled babble) · MARGE:\n960\t\"That bear's on the ice all game. Treat him like furniture.\" [IGNORE THE BEAR / HUNT THE BEAR] · MARGE: \"And win or\n961\ttie, the mall's got a Shootout Showcase after. Mall money. We want it.\"\n962\t*Post*: GLITTERMAN: \"Fine. The Final. My Grizzlies. My Dome. My rules.\" · SNIPES: \"Your Dome's gonna need a new roof.\"\n963\t\n964\t*Chapter 5 pre-game (the Dome's tunnel, then the spotlight intro)*: STERLING: \"I've never lost. Not once. Not even\n965\tat Go Fish.\" · SNIPES: \"There's a first time for everything, Goldilocks.\" · THE VAULT: \"…\" · LEMMY: \"He's very big,\n966\tPipesy.\" · MARGE: \"Forty-six years behind that bench. I've seen better teams. Prettier teams. Teams that could spell.\"\n967\t· MARGE: \"Never saw one that wanted it more. Go make it go KABOOM.\" · [DORIS EARLY / DORIS LATE]\n968\t*In-game*: when the Grizzlies' Gilded Boost starts, GLITTERMAN on the jumbotron: \"Synergy, boys!\" When Doris\n969\tplays, MARGE: \"DORIS! PLAY THE SONG!\" (the organ's charge fanfare, the crowd claps, the boost).\n970\t*Post (win), the ending*: the handshake line (both teams) → Dunny lifts the Kaboom Cup, which goes off in a confetti\n971\texplosion. CHUCK: \"THE KABOOM CUP IS… KA-BOOMING!\" → GLITTERMAN: \"My parking meters…\" → MARGE: \"Bylaw 1897-B, Goldie.\n972\tLook it up.\" → GUS: \"Yep.\" → the Flood Wagon drives a lap with the team on top → **credits** over the run's highlight\n973\treplays (7.16), then Coach Marge: \"Same time next year.\" → the title, with the **Cup on display** in the Icebox from\n974\tthen on.\n975\t\n976\t**Unlocks** (15 stars in all; exhibition cheats): 3★ Big Heads (`headR` × 1.8) · 6★ Octopus Rain · 9★ Glow Puck · 12★\n977\tAlways KABOOM (for humans) · 15★ Retro Rigs (`style: 'classic'`). Finishing the story makes the Gilded Grizzlies and\n978\tThe Vault playable in exhibition and adds the Cup to the title screen.\n979\t\n980\t### 11.4 Practice: Coach Marge's Drills (at the Ol' Icebox, house lights half on)\n981\t| # | Drill | Pass condition | Teaches |\n982\t|---|---|---|---|\n983\t| 1 | Wheels | skate through 6 gates in order in 25 s (one gate wants a hockey stop) | skating, turbo, stops |\n984\t| 2 | Tape to Tape | 5 completed passes to moving teammates + 1 saucer over a sled | passes, saucers, aim |\n985\t| 3 | Top Shelf | hit 4 corner targets on an empty net (wrist and slap) | shots, aim, lift |\n986\t| 4 | One-Timers | 3 one-timer goals on Lemmy from Dunny's cross-crease feeds | one-timers |\n987\t| 5 | Finish Your Check | big-hit 3 training dummies into the glass and break a panel | checks, turbo hits, glass |\n988\t| 6 | Gloves Off | win a spar with Big Lou (he goes easy) | the fight controls |\n989\t| 7 | KABOOM! | with a full meter, score with a KABOOM shot and survive Lou's KABOOM check | KABOOM mode |\n990\t\n991\tEach drill opens with a Marge line (voiced) and a prompt panel with glyph chips, tracks its counter in the HUD, and\n992\tsaves its completion. Completing all 7 earns the \"Marge Approved\" badge (Records). Chapter 1 offers drills 1–3 as\n993\tits warm-up.\n994\t\n995\t### 11.5 Text pools (in `07-data-text.js`; sizes are the minimums)\n996\tCommentary: 18 event types × 4–8 lines (≈ 110 lines) plus 20 Moose filler anecdotes; chirps: 30; tips: 14;\n997\tthree-stars lines: 12; loss pep talks: 5; menu blurbs: 1 per item; About pages (12.1). Appendix D has samples for each.\n998\t\n999\t---\n1000\t\n1001\t## 12. Screens and flows (10-foot UI)\n1002\t\n1003\t**Rules for every screen**: at most 6 choices visible; big tiles and cards; one line of help; a legend at the bottom\n1004\twith glyph chips (`{pass} SELECT  {deke} BACK`, as keycaps or mouse icons for keyboard and mouse). D-pad, stick,\n1005\tarrows and WASD move focus; ✕ / Enter / Space pick; ○ / Esc / Backspace go back. **The mouse hovering a tile focuses\n1006\tit and a click picks it.** Focus has an animated gold border, a slight scale-up and an organ blip. No dense tables\n1007\tanywhere: stats are a few big numbers.\n1008\t\n1009\t1. **Title**: the Ol' Icebox at night, spotlights sweeping the ice, two teams skating lazily (AI). The logo slams in\n1010\t   with an explosion and the horn, then `PRESS ANY BUTTON` (`TAP` is never shown; see 15.2). Then the main menu: 6 tiles\n1011\t   in 2 rows: **CUP RUN** (Continue/New when a save exists), **EXHIBITION**, **PRACTICE**, **RECORDS**, **SETTINGS**\n1012\t   (the engine's settings screen: `game.menu('settings')`), **ABOUT**. The version label (`E.versionLabel()` + the\n1013\t   game's version) sits small in a corner, and the engine corner buttons stay at the top right.\n1014\t2. **Exhibition → Sides**: every joined player is a token in the middle column (CPU); push left or right to join HOME\n1015\t   or AWAY; ✕ to ready. \"Press START on a free controller, or 2 on the keyboard, to join\" (`game.allowJoin({ max: 4\n1016\t   })`). The keyboard halves show their keys. Mouse: click HOME or AWAY to move the keyboard player's token.\n1017\t3. **Exhibition → Setup**: 3 big cards side by side: HOME team, ARENA, AWAY team (left/right on a focused card cycles\n1018\t   it; each team card shows its logo ×3, name, and 4 pip bars: Speed, Shooting, Hitting, Goalie). Below, one row of\n1019\t   option chips: Periods (1/2/3), Period length (1:00 / 1:30 / 2:00 / 3:00 / 4:00), Difficulty, Cheats (unlocked\n1020\t   ones). **FACE OFF!** starts.\n1021\t4. **Story map**: the bus on a snowy highway with 5 stops (each a town sign with its logo and earned stars). The stop\n1022\t   in focus shows the chapter title and objectives. Click a stop to pick it.\n1023\t5. **Cutscene**: the set (the locker room or rink-side), characters staged, `E.Dialog` boxes with live portraits,\n1024\t   babble and typed text; choices are 2 big options. ✕ advances; holding ○ for 1 s skips the scene (with a fill ring).\n1025\t6. **Pre-game card**: matchup logos, the arena, the objectives with ★ slots, the tactic chosen. ✕ FACE OFF.\n1026\t7. **Match** (HUD 7.18). **Pause** (engine): Resume, Objectives & Info (the story objectives, or the exhibition's\n1027\t   setup), Restart Game, **Dev Mode**, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title.\n1028\t8. **Intermission**: the period summary card (goals, shots, hits: big numbers), then `{pass} DRIVE THE FLOOD WAGON`\n1029\t   or `{deke} SKIP`.\n1030\t9. **Results**: the final score huge, the **three stars** revealed one by one (portrait cards, a stat line, a\n1031\t   commentary line), the objectives ticking ★, then CONTINUE / REMATCH / MAIN MENU.\n1032\t10. **Records**: big numbers with a label each: Hardest Shot (km/h = u/s ÷ 16 × 3.6), Biggest Hit, Most Goals in a\n1033\t    Game, Fights Won, KABOOMs, Story Stars x/15, Drills x/7. Two pages at most.\n1034\t11. **About**: section 12.1's pages, paged with L1/R1, left/right or a click on the arrows.\n1035\t12. **Credits**: the end roll over highlight replays.\n1036\t\n1037\t### 12.1 About / Credits screen\n1038\tPages (at most 8 lines each, in the large font): **Credits** (game design and code: Claude Opus 5.5, `claude-opus-5-5`,\n1039\tfor Michael Crosato's cc-matrix; engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2, MIT; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; every sound, voice and\n1040\tsong synthesized in code; asset-store props from CC0 sets, listed by name) · **Source Information** (every field TASK.md\n1041\tlists) · **Testing Feedback** · **Engine Feedback** · **Prompt Feedback** · **Engine changes** (the summary of\n1042\tENGINE-CHANGES.md). The builder fills the feedback pages at the end with the same text as the chat reply and\n1043\t`exit-interview.json`, writing \"unknown\" for anything that can't be confirmed.\n1044\t\n1045\t---\n1046\t\n1047\t## 13. Settings (via `menu.settings`; the engine's Display, Sound, Comfort and Controls stay)\n1048\tButton symbols (PlayStation / Xbox) · Difficulty (Rookie / Pro / All-Star / Legend) · Period length (exhibition default)\n1049\t· Camera (Broadcast / Overhead) · Camera distance (Near / Normal / Far) · Commentary (On / Off) · Subtitles (On / Off) ·\n1050\tVoices volume · Crowd volume · Player intros (On / Off) · Replays (Auto / Off) · Flood Wagon (Ask / Always / Never) ·\n1051\tPuck trail (Off / Streak / Glow) · Tips (On / Off) · Reset tips. Every one is read live.\n1052\t\n1053\t---\n1054\t\n1055\t## 14. Online: AI Hub sessions (`Net`, shared-world)\n1056\t\n1057\t### 14.1 Page tags (in `<head>`, after the session client)\n1058\t```html\n1059\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n1060\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n1061\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n1062\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n1063\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Outscore the other team in one 3-minute period\">\n1064\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD skate · ✕/J pass · □/K shoot · ○/L deke · R2/Shift turbo\">\n1065\t<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n1066\t<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n1067\t```\n1068\t\n1069\t### 14.2 Flow (when `AIHub.active`)\n1070\t1. There is no title, attract or menu. Boot first calls\n1071\t   `info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If `info` is null, carry on\n1072\t   exactly as outside a session. Otherwise it picks the teams and the arena (step 2), builds the arena, and calls\n1073\t   `AIHub.ready()` (step 4).\n1074\t2. **Teams**: even seats (0, 2) are HOME and odd seats (1, 3) AWAY; with one player, that player is HOME vs the CPU.\n1075\t   The two teams and the arena are picked by `AIHub.rng('setup')`, the same on every copy; the host's first snapshot\n1076\t   confirms them. The CPU fills the rest. In a 2v1, the lone human's CPU teammates get AI skill +.15.\n1077\t3. **Our own card** (scene `session`, until `start`): the arena at night with spotlights; each player's skater lined\n1078\t   up on their team's blue line with a nameplate in their seat color (names sanitized for the pixel font, drawn on\n1079\t   the canvas, never put into HTML); \"HOW TO WIN: Outscore the other team in one 3-minute period\"; THIS PLAYER'S\n1080\t   CONTROLS as glyph chips for their device; a ✓ on each ready player; the countdown from the `card` event. Enter or\n1081\t   ✕ (button 0), or a click or tap on READY, calls `AIHub.answer('ready')`. △ (button 3), T, or a click on MORE TIME\n1082\t   calls `AIHub.answer('more')` (pressing again takes it back). The card changes nothing in the round.\n1083\t4. Call `AIHub.ready()` once the arena is built, with no key press.\n1084\t5. On `start`, show a big 3–2–1 while `AIHub.time() < 0`, then a faceoff at time 0. The match config is 1 period of\n1085\t   3:00, then sudden-death OT capped at 1:00, then a tie. Replays are 3 s, there are no intros and no Flood Wagon;\n1086\t   fights and items are on.\n1087\t6. **The host** (`info.isHost`) runs `Match.step` with all CPU AI and the remote players' intents. It calls\n1088\t   `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` exactly once: at the final horn, on `time-up` (at once, with\n1089\t   the current score), or when a round that began with 2+ players is down to one human (`leave`; the leavers are left\n1090\t   out of the standings). Standings list the winning team's remaining players in one array and the losers in the\n1091\t   next; a tie puts everyone in one array. With 1 player,\n1092\t   `standings: [[id]]` and `won: true | false`. `scores` maps each id to their own points (goals + assists); `stats`\n1093\t   maps each id to `{ Goals, Assists, Hits, Fights }`; `awards` are the three stars that are humans\n1094\t   (`{ id, title: '1st Star', detail }`).\n1095\t7. **Leaving**: a human who leaves becomes a CPU skater. The hub voids the round when the host leaves.\n1096\t8. On `end`: stop input and sound (`audio.music(null)`, mute), freeze on the final score, and send nothing more.\n1097\t9. **No pausing in a session**: the gameplay scene is not `pausable` and `autoPause` is off. Options (or Esc) opens a\n1098\t   small non-pausing overlay (Sound, Music, Voices, Button symbols, Camera, Back), during which the local skater\n1099\t   coasts. There is no Quit, Restart or Dev Mode. Create + Options belongs to the hub (engine patch 2). Use no\n1100\t   `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt` or `window.open`, and no network but the hub.\n1101\t10. **Server copies** (`info.server`: the host with no player): they run the same host code with no local input or\n1102\t    camera and draw only a small \"HOSTING\" line.\n1103\t\n1104\t### 14.3 Netcode (it stays within 20 messages a second per copy and 16 KB per message)\n1105\t- **Clients → host**, 15 Hz, unreliable, `{ t: 'in', s: seq, at: AIHub.time() rounded, mx, my (×100 rounded),\n1106\t  h: bits (shoot, lob, turbo), c: [pass, shoot, deke, lob, chirp, switch] press counters (mod 256), ax, ay (aim, or\n1107\t  omitted) }`. The host turns counter differences into presses, so a lost packet loses no taps, and treats the\n1108\t  latest packet as held state. The host acknowledges with `ack` per player.\n1109\t- **Host → all**, 15 Hz, unreliable, under 1,200 bytes: `{ t: 's', n: tick, at, ph: phase code, p: period,\n1110\t  k: clock ×10, sc: [h, a], b: [boomH, boomA, kaboomFlags], pk: [x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, owner], e: [[id, x, y, vx, vy,\n1111\t  facing (0–255), state code, stateT ×10, flags], × 8 (6 skaters + 2 goalies)], ack: { playerId: seq }, it: items,\n1112\t  f: fight state (when fighting), ev: [recent events with ids, each repeated in 4 snapshots] }`. Integers only.\n1113\t- **Reliable host messages** (rare): `setup` (teams, arena, seat → skater map), `phase` changes (goal, period end,\n1114\t  final, fight start and end), and `glass` and `hole` state changes.\n1115\t- **Clients render** others interpolated about 120 ms behind the newest snapshot (two snapshot intervals less a\n1116\t  margin; tune it with the harness's latency and jitter settings). **Their own skater is predicted**: it\n1117\t  starts from the snapshot's authoritative state at `ack`, re-applies the pending intents with `Skater.skateStep`\n1118\t  (ignoring collisions), and blends the drawn position toward the result over 0.1 s, snapping when off by more than\n1119\t  48. While the client's skater owns the puck, the puck is drawn at its predicted blade. Each client plays effects,\n1120\t  sounds and commentary from the snapshot events it receives (deduplicated by id); the host sends commentary line ids\n1121\t  inside the events. Instant replays run on each copy from its own snapshot history.\n1122\t- **Budget**: the host sends 15 snapshots a second plus a few reliable messages, so it stays under 20/s. Each client\n1123\t  sends 15 inputs a second plus rare reliable messages.\n1124\t\n1125\t---\n1126\t\n1127\t## 15. Attract mode, touch-only devices and dev mode\n1128\t\n1129\t### 15.1 Attract mode (scene `attract`)\n1130\t- **Idle timer** on title, menus, side select, setup, the story map, records and about: 10 s without any input (keys,\n1131\t  buttons, clicks, wheel, a mouse move of more than 8 px, a stick or trigger past .3) → `game.go('attract', null,\n1132\t  { fade: 'dissolve' })`. Not during cutscenes, matches or the engine's open menus, and never in sessions.\n1133\t- **The reel**: a script (`game.script`) of segments, each built on the real match simulation with every skater on\n1134\t  AI, cheats free (infinite turbo, forced events, warping the puck or players). Each loop picks a new arena and teams.\n1135\t  1. *Puck Drop* (8 s): the intro spotlights, a faceoff, play.\n1136\t  2. *Big Hits* (8 s): a forced turbo big hit into the glass, which shatters.\n1137\t  3. *Highlight Goal* (12 s): a set-up 2-on-1, a cross-crease pass, a one-timer goal, the horn and the instant replay.\n1138\t  4. *Gloves Off* (10 s): an AI-vs-AI fight to a knockdown.\n1139\t  5. *KABOOM!* (10 s): forced KABOOM mode, a KABOOM shot that blasts the goalie into the net.\n1140\t  6. *Fan Frenzy* (7 s): items thrown and grabbed; an octopus slip.\n1141\t  7. *Story teaser* (8 s): 3 cutscene lines with portraits and babble.\n1142\t  8. *Flood Wagon* (6 s): the AI driver resurfacing scuffed ice.\n1143\t  9. *Records card* (5 s): the logo, `PRESS ANY BUTTON`, and the top records.\n1144\t  The loop is about 75 s, then it starts again.\n1145\t- **Overlay**: a `DEMO` tag, the logo bug, and `PRESS ANY BUTTON` (glyph per device) blinking. On touch-only devices\n1146\t  it reads \"Controller or keyboard required\" instead.\n1147\t- **Any input** ends it: back to the title with that input consumed (`input.consumeAll()`), so it triggers nothing\n1148\t  else. The audio follows the settings (browsers stay silent until a first gesture anyway).\n1149\t\n1150\t### 15.2 Touch-only devices\n1151\t- **Detection**: `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches`, no gamepad\n1152\t  seen, and no key pressed since load. Re-check on `gamepadconnected` and the first `keydown`; either one switches to\n1153\t  normal at once.\n1154\t- **Touch-only**: no touch controls anywhere (`touch: []` on every scene, the engine's touch buttons hidden). The title\n1155\t  shows a large banner, \"Controller or keyboard required\", and a big **SETTINGS** button (a tap opens\n1156\t  `game.menu('settings')`); the engine's corner menu button stays. Taps don't start the game. The attract mode runs by\n1157\t  the same 10 s rule, and taps don't leave it (only to open Settings).\n1158\t\n1159\t### 15.3 Dev mode (scene overlay `Dev`, from the pause menu's **Dev Mode** item; also `#dev`)\n1160\t- Choosing it closes the engine's pause menu and opens the Dev panel. While the panel is open the match holds its own\n1161\t  `devPause` flag (the engine's `game.paused` is false, so the panel can read input), unless **Live** is toggled on: the panel docks to the right at 45% width and the game runs behind it, so slider\n1162\t  changes show at once.\n1163\t- **Navigation**: L1/R1 (or Tab, or a click) switch tabs; up/down move; left/right adjust (hold to accelerate; L2/R2\n1164\t  ×10 steps); △ (or R) resets the row; **RESET ALL TO DEFAULTS** is the first row of TUNING; ○ / Esc closes. The mouse\n1165\t  hovers to focus rows, drags sliders and clicks toggles. Each row shows its value and its default.\n1166\t- **TUNING** tab: every `T` key with a slider (Appendix A), grouped Skating, Puck & Passing, Shooting, Goalies,\n1167\t  Hitting, AI, BOOM & Items, Fights, Match. Values persist in `E.store('dev:tuning')`. **Log tuning** prints a JSON of\n1168\t  the non-default values to the console, for designers.\n1169\t- **CHEATS**: infinite turbo; god mode (no knockdowns); always KABOOM; puck magnet (the puck comes to the human's\n1170\t  blade); freeze AI; CPU goalies off; big heads; octopus rain; glow puck; retro rigs; instant BOOM full (an action).\n1171\t- **WARP**: start any chapter or cutscene; jump to period 2, 3 or OT, or the shootout; set the clock to 0:10; score\n1172\t  +1 for home or away; win or lose this game now; spawn each item or hazard at center; start a fight; start KABOOM;\n1173\t  break the thin ice; shatter a panel; trigger the Flood Wagon; go to results, attract, about or the lab.\n1174\t- **DEBUG**: overlays (bodies and radii, blade points, AI roles and targets, the puck's predicted path, goalie save\n1175\t  shapes, grudge numbers, rig skeletons via `rig.debug(r)`), FPS, slow motion (1, .5, .25), frame step (paused: ✕\n1176\t  advances one step), free camera (the stick pans, the triggers zoom), hide the HUD (screenshot mode), the RNG seed,\n1177\t  and a **sound test** (play every sfx, song, layer, organ sting and voice, including a babble line per character).\n1178\t- **Not available in AI Hub sessions.**\n1179\t\n1180\t---\n1181\t\n1182\t## 16. Build order and milestones\n1183\tBuild in this order. Each milestone ends with its tests passing (`node tests/run.mjs`) and a look at its screenshots.\n1184\tThe game must be playable from M3 on.\n1185\t\n1186\t| M | Deliverable | Acceptance |\n1187\t|---|---|---|\n1188\t| **M0 Setup** | dev folder, the engine copied, the vendor files, `tools/build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` running an empty suite, `src/` skeleton, a title scene that boots in the browser and headless, ENGINE-CHANGES.md started | the built HTML opens from `file://` with no errors (`tools/check.mjs`); the headless boot test passes |\n1189\t| **M1 Rink, skating, rigs** | `Rink` geometry and drawing (ice, lines, boards, glass panels, nets, benches), the floor TileMap, `skateStep`, SkaterRig (stride, glide, stop, crossovers, stick idle), the broadcast camera, the animation lab | unit tests for geometry and skating; filmstrips of stride and stop look right; screenshots of the Icebox rink in all 3 views |\n1190\t| **M2 Puck play** | the puck, possession, stick-handling, passes (lead, saucer), one-timers, wrist and slap shots, goal detection, posts, net bulge, Goalie v1 (positioning, save solver, rebounds, freeze), HOCKEY_KEYS, mouse and right-stick aim, glyph chips, font patch, HUD v1 | headless: a pass reaches a stationary and a moving mate; a shot into an empty net scores; a shot at the goalie is saved; a post hit emits `post`; glyph labels per device |\n1191\t| **M3 First playable match** | Match flow (faceoffs, clock, stoppages, goals, celebrations, periods, final, results, three stars), team AI, the referee, the crowd v1, audio v1 (sfx, the horn, the organ, the crowd bed, the theme), Exhibition Setup (1 player) | AI vs AI plays 3 periods with no errors and 3–12 goals; a bot-driven human match (the bot of 18.3) completes; `balance.mjs` runs |\n1192\t| **M4 Over the top** | checks, knockdowns, the glass, turbo, deke, poke, BOOM and KABOOM, items and hazards, chirps, commentary with babble voices, instant replay, Fx | headless: the big-hit threshold, glass crack then shatter, KABOOM start, shot and end, item effects, replay playback ends and returns to a faceoff |\n1193\t| **M5 Fights, OT, multiplayer, menus** | fights and the sin bin, OT and the shootout (manual goalie), local 1–4 players and side select, all 10-foot menus, settings, records, about | headless: a fight from gloves to a winner and the sin bin timer; a shootout to a decision; 4 inputs each moving their own skater; mouse hover focus and click in menus (browser) |\n1194\t| **M6 Story and content** | all 5 arenas dressed (lights, props, crowds, hazards), all 6 teams, the story map, the cutscene runner and every script, choices, objectives, stars and unlocks, the Flood Wagon minigame, the 7 practice drills, the boss (The Vault, Golden Twister, Gilded Mode, Boost and organ), the ending and credits with highlights, saves | the whole-story playthrough test passes (18.3); screenshots of every arena and every cutscene set |\n1195\t| **M7 Attract, touch, dev** | the attract reel, idle detection, touch-only mode, the Dev panel (all 4 tabs), the sound test | headless: idle 10 s → attract; all 9 segments visited; any input → title; dev slider change and reset; browser: a touch-only emulation shows the banner and attract runs |\n1196\t| **M8 AI Hub** | `Net` (connect, card, host and client, prediction, events, finish), the metas, session flow | the fake-hub headless test (18.5) passes; the real harness passes in all 4 configurations (18.6) |\n1197\t| **M9 Polish and balance** | tuning passes with `balance.mjs`, act on `check.mjs` look notes, every screenshot reviewed at 1280×720 and 1920×1080, the About pages and `exit-interview.json` filled in, the final build | the full `node tests/run.mjs` is green; no TODO or placeholder strings; `exit-interview.json` parses; the HTML runs from `file://` with no network requests |\n1198\t\n1199\t---\n1200\t\n1201\t## 17. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1202\t| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n1203\t|---|---|---|\n1204\t| Skater and stick animation | new motion on a procedural rig decides whether it reads as hockey | built first (M1) in the animation lab; filmstrip every motion; keep solvePose overrides small and data-driven; fall back to the engine's poses for rare states |\n1205\t| Puck feel (possession, passes, one-timers) | the core of the fun; easy to get floaty or sticky | every constant a slider from day one; headless pass and shot tests; play it at M2 before building on it |\n1206\t| Goalie believability | too good is frustrating, too weak is boring | a physical save solver (reaction, lateral speed, shapes) rather than dice; `balance.mjs` shoots 200 shots per type and checks the save-rate bands in 7.6 |\n1207\t| Curved boards, glass and depth sorting | custom drawing in a tile engine | far boards as background, end and corner panels queued per panel, near boards cut low; screenshots in all views at M1 |\n1208\t| Netcode under latency, loss and limits | shared world, 20 msgs/s, unreliable packets | a pure `skateStep` for prediction; press counters; snapshots under 1,200 bytes (a test asserts it); a fake hub in Node with latency and loss before the real harness |\n1209\t| Hub compliance | a session fails the harness's checklist | follow 14.2 step by step; the harness at M8 in all 4 configurations; no pause, quit or dialogs in sessions |\n1210\t| Audio quality (babble, horn, organ) | voices can sound like noise | the sound test in Dev from M4; tune formants by ear; keep the voice bus quieter than the sfx bus |\n1211\t| PlayStation glyphs in the pixel font | they rendered as `?` | the font patch plus glyph chips at M2; a test renders each chip |\n1212\t| Scope | a big demo | milestones in value order; data-driven content; the systems shared by story, drills, attract and sessions (all are `Match` configs) |\n1213\t| Determinism (replays, tests, attract) | hidden `Math.random` use | only `RNG.sim` in the simulation; a test runs the same seed twice and compares a state hash |\n1214\t\n1215\t---\n1216\t\n1217\t## 18. Testing\n1218\t\n1219\t**One command**: `node tests/run.mjs` builds, then runs every suite in order and prints **only failures** plus one\n1220\tline: `ICE HOC-KABOOM TESTS: 214 passed, 0 failed (headless 9 suites, browser 3, hub 4) in 182 s`.\n1221\t`--quick` runs only the headless suites; `--only <suite>` reruns one (after changing the code it covers). Headless\n1222\tsuites load `build/game.js` into a `vm` context with the stand-ins from `engine/kits/test.mjs` (`window`,\n1223\t`addEventListener`, `location`). They drive the game with `game.advance`, `input.tap` and `input.hold`, and read\n1224\t`game.debug.snapshot()`. No subagents or workflows review anything; the scripts decide.\n1225\t\n1226\t### 18.1 Unit (pure functions)\n1227\tRink inside, normal and clamp at corners; the faceoff dot table; `skateStep` (time to top speed, stop distance, turn\n1228\tradius at speed, turbo drain); puck friction distance; board reflection angles; post ping; goal-line crossing (inside\n1229\tvs post); pass lead hits a moving mate; shot aim stays inside the mouth for σ = 0; save-shape tests; impulse\n1230\tthresholds; BOOM gain table; fight damage and stamina; tuning reset and resetAll; the glyph label per device and\n1231\tsetting; the name sanitizer; snapshot encode, decode and size (< 1,200 bytes for 8 entities, 3 items and 4 events);\n1232\tinput packet press counters across a dropped packet; objective predicates.\n1233\t\n1234\t### 18.2 Systems (headless game)\n1235\t- A faceoff leads to possession within 2 s.\n1236\t- A scripted wrist shot from the slot at an empty net scores.\n1237\t- A slapshot at the goalie from the blue line is saved.\n1238\t- A one-timer cross-crease scores at least 4 of 10 seeded tries.\n1239\t- A turbo check at full speed knocks down; a second hit into the same panel shatters it, and the puck leaves through\n1240\t  it → a faceoff.\n1241\t- Holding △ near a rival with a grudge starts a fight; scripted jabs win it; the loser is in the sin bin for 20 s; a\n1242\t  power-play banner shows.\n1243\t- Filling BOOM starts KABOOM; a KABOOM shot blasts the goalie; it ends after 15 s.\n1244\t- Each item applies its effect and expires; thin ice breaks after a big hit; a skater in a hole is frozen 3 s.\n1245\t- The period ends at 0:00 → intermission → the next period; OT is sudden death; the shootout reaches a decision.\n1246\t- Results show three stars.\n1247\t- 4 local players each move only their own skater.\n1248\t- Replay plays and returns.\n1249\t- The same seed and inputs twice give the same state hash after 60 s (determinism).\n1250\t\n1251\t### 18.3 Scripted playthrough of the whole game (`tests/play-story.mjs`)\n1252\tFrom boot: title → CUP RUN → for chapters 1 to 5: advance the cutscene (tap confirm; take choice 1 in chapters 1, 3\n1253\tand 5, choice 2 in 2 and 4), run warm-up drills 1–3 in chapter 1 by script, then play the match with **the bot\n1254\tcontrolling the human team's skater through `game.input`** (the CPU intent turned into stick and buttons, as in the\n1255\tSPORTS kit's `bot()`), with dev tuning giving the home team AI skill .95 and the rivals .3 so each game is won in real\n1256\tplay. Play 1 period for real, then warp the clock to 0:05 for the remaining periods, keeping the lead. Play the\n1257\tintermission Flood Wagon once with the bot steering, the chapter 4 Shootout Showcase, and the chapter 5 boss phases\n1258\t(the Boost and organ events must fire). Then the post-game, results, the map, the ending, credits and back to the\n1259\ttitle. Assert at each stage: the expected scene and chapter, at least one goal per game, no errors, stars recorded,\n1260\tthe save written, and every chapter's new mechanic event seen (one-timer, kaboom_start, thin_ice_break, fight_end,\n1261\tmascot_down, shootout_end, vault_cracked or a boss goal). If real play hasn't produced a chapter's signature event by\n1262\tthe end of its first period, trigger it with the Dev warp (`game.debug.warp('breakIce')` and the like), then assert\n1263\tthat the game handled it (its consequences, commentary and objective). Also play **Practice drills 1–7** by script and\n1264\tassert each passes.\n1265\t\n1266\t### 18.4 Other headless suites\n1267\t- **Attract**: idle 10 s from the title → attract; run 80 s; all 9 segments visited; tapping confirm → title with\n1268\t  the input consumed.\n1269\t- **Dev**: open from the pause menu item; change 3 sliders (the values apply to the match); reset one; reset all\n1270\t  (all defaults); a cheat toggles; warps work.\n1271\t- **Exhibition**: 60 s with 4 players, each scheme.\n1272\t- **Balance** (`balance.mjs`; it also prints a table when run alone): 20 AI-vs-AI games at Pro, averaging 5–10 goals\n1273\t  a game; save % .78–.90; at least 2 fights per 10 games; KABOOM 1–4 per game; plus 7.6's shot-type bands.\n1274\t- **Text**: every TEXT pool meets its minimum; every `{token}` resolves; no line wider than its box at scale 1.\n1275\t\n1276\t### 18.5 Fake-hub network test (headless, Node)\n1277\tTwo to four `vm` contexts, each with the engine, the game and a fake `AIHub` (an in-memory bus with configurable\n1278\tlatency 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss). It runs connect → card (scripted ready) → start → 60 s of scripted play → time-up.\n1279\tAssert: the host's and clients' scores match; a client's own-skater error stays below 12 u on average; presses are\n1280\tnever lost; `finish` is called once with valid standings; a leaving client's skater turns CPU; a server-mode host\n1281\tworks.\n1282\t\n1283\t### 18.6 Browser suites (Playwright 1.63, Chromium; `TMPDIR` set)\n1284\t- `engine/tools/check.mjs` on the built HTML and on `#match/muskrats/drillers/icebox`, `#fight` and `#kaboom`: no\n1285\t  errors, and every look note handled.\n1286\t- **Menus and input**: keyboard navigation through the main menu; mouse hover moves focus and a click picks;\n1287\t  `lastDevice` changes switch the prompt chips; Settings → Xbox changes the chips.\n1288\t- **Touch-only**: `--size 390x844@3` with coarse-pointer emulation shows the banner and SETTINGS, and attract starts\n1289\t  after 10 s.\n1290\t- **Hub harness**: serve `dev/hub/` (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, confirm the page title, kill by\n1291\t  PID afterwards). Open `harness.html?game=game.html&players=2&auto=1`; then\n1292\t  `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; then the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; then\n1293\t  `&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Each waits for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and asserts\n1294\t  `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, printing the failed checks otherwise. Then the game outside a session still\n1295\t  reaches the title.\n1296\t\n1297\t### 18.7 Screenshots (only for what scripts can't judge; `tests/shots.mjs`)\n1298\tAt 1280×720 and 1920×1080: title, the attract segments, side select with 4 players, setup, every arena at a faceoff,\n1299\ta big hit and shattered glass, a fight, KABOOM mode, a goal celebration, a replay, results with three stars, a\n1300\tcutscene with a portrait, the story map, a drill, the Flood Wagon, the Dev panel, Settings with Xbox glyphs, the\n1301\tAbout pages, the session card (from the harness), and the touch-only banner at 390×844. Look at every one, comparing\n1302\tagainst the look target (8) and the 10-foot rules (12).\n1303\t\n1304\t---\n1305\t\n1306\t## 19. Definition of done (TASK.md → where it is met)\n1307\t- [ ] Genre and perspective chosen and used (0, 7.15). Title from a real RNG (0).\n1308\t- [ ] Single HTML with the given name, the dev folder, no network requests (1).\n1309\t- [ ] Built on the handoff engine; changes logged (4) and summarized in About.\n1310\t- [ ] Native look with new hockey art (8); native animation with new hockey motion (9).\n1311\t- [ ] All audio in code; gibberish voices (10).\n1312\t- [ ] AI Hub sessions passing the harness, plus local multiplayer for the game on its own (14, 6.1, 12).\n1313\t- [ ] Feature-complete demo: story, exhibition, practice, records and every mechanic shown in play, drills and attract\n1314\t      (11, 12, 15.1).\n1315\t- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu with live sliders and reset to defaults (15.3).\n1316\t- [ ] Attract mode after 10 s idle on title and menus; any input exits (15.1).\n1317\t- [ ] 10-foot, controller-first UI; native keyboard and mouse (aim, hover focus, click); prompts follow the last\n1318\t      device; PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option (6, 12).\n1319\t- [ ] Touch-only: \"Controller or keyboard required\", the settings button, attract runs (15.2).\n1320\t- [ ] Narrative tone: hockey broadcast and small-town hockey comedy (11.3, Appendix D).\n1321\t- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubs (a test enforces it).\n1322\t- [ ] Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in the chat reply **and** the About\n1323\t      screen; `exit-interview.json` in TASK.md's exact shape, parsing as JSON. Suggested `aiHub` values: name\n1324\t      \"Ice Hoc-Kaboom\"; tagline \"Over-the-top 3-on-3 arcade hockey\"; description \"Glass-shattering hits, dropped\n1325\t      gloves and explosive KABOOM slapshots as the Mukluk Falls Muskrats fight to save their rink. Story, exhibition\n1326\t      and up to four players.\"; type \"Game\"; genre \"Sports\"; source \"Ice hockey\"; series \"\"; players \"1–4\"; controls\n1327\t      \"Stick/WASD skate · ✕/J pass · □/K shoot · ○/L deke · △/I saucer & gloves · R2/Shift turbo\"; tags\n1328\t      `[\"arcade\", \"sports\", \"versus\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\", \"story\"]`. The Source Information `plan` field is\n1329\t      `PLAN.md`.\n1330\t\n1331\t---\n1332\t\n1333\t## Appendix A: Tuning defaults (`T`; every row is a Dev slider)\n1334\t| Group | Key | Default | Min–max | Meaning |\n1335\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1336\t| Skating | skateMax | 132 | 80–200 | top speed (u/s) at rating 3 |\n1337\t| | skateAccel | 300 | 120–600 | acceleration |\n1338\t| | iceGlide | 28 | 0–120 | coasting deceleration |\n1339\t| | turnSlow / turnFast | 5.0 / 2.6 | 1–10 | rad/s at low and top speed |\n1340\t| | edgeGrip | 6 | 1–20 | sideways decay /s |\n1341\t| | stopDecel | 700 | 300–1400 | hockey-stop deceleration |\n1342\t| | turboMul | 1.45 | 1–2 | turbo speed factor |\n1343\t| | turboDrain / turboRegen | 0.45 / 0.18 | 0–2 | meter per second |\n1344\t| Puck & passing | puckFriction / puckDrag | 26 / 0.12 | 0–80 / 0–.5 | puck deceleration |\n1345\t| | boardBounce | 0.62 | .2–1 | boards restitution |\n1346\t| | pickupRadius | 8 | 4–16 | blade pickup |\n1347\t| | passMin / passMax | 240 / 420 | 150–600 | pass speeds |\n1348\t| | saucerApex | 10 | 4–24 | saucer height |\n1349\t| Shooting | wristSpeed | 330 | 200–500 | wrist shot |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de63938e-b4cc-4b63-8e8c-4cc91a6c7b2f","uuid":"e1d1206b-ef59-4f01-b4b0-0fbb0f925ad3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:51:11.739Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-055058__x9a2bbb/work/PLAN.md","content":"played with a straight face, chirps that rhyme, and big heart. PG: no blood, no slurs, no swearing (a beep and\nbabble stand in for \"a curse word\").\n\n**Chapter flow**: storymap (a snowy highway map; the team bus drives between 5 town stops, each showing its stars and\nlock) → pre-game cutscene (with one choice) → [chapter 1: optional warm-up drills 1–3] → player intros → the game (its\nobjectives listed on the pause screen and a pre-game card) → intermission Flood Wagon (offered) → post-game cutscene →\nresults and three stars → stars and unlocks → back to the map. **A loss**: a short Marge pep talk (a different one for\neach chapter, in TEXT) and Retry or Back to Map. Progress autosaves (`game.saves`) after each chapter and choice.\n\n**Choices** (one per chapter; they set the game's team tactic, 7.13): chapter 1 \"Clean and fast\" (Finesse) / \"Mean and\nloud\" (Grit); chapter 2 the same two; chapter 3 \"Let Lou loose\" (Lou Fgt +1, fights likelier) / \"Keep it on the ice\" (Lou\nPas +1); chapter 4 \"Ignore the bear\" / \"Hunt the bear\" (the AI targets Polar Pete); chapter 5 \"Doris plays early\"\n(the organ boost at the start of the 2nd period) / \"Doris plays late\" (at 5:00 left in the 3rd, +50% stronger).\n\n| # | Chapter | Arena / rival / rules | New mechanic spotlighted | Objectives (★ each) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Home Opener** | Ol' Icebox vs Dryfork Drillers, 3 × 1:30; the rivals play one difficulty step below the setting (never below Rookie) | skating, passing, shooting, one-timers, checking, BOOM meter, Flood Wagon | Win · Score a one-timer · Land 3 big hits |\n| 2 | **Pond Rules** | Lake Kabonk vs Logjam Lumberjacks, 3 × 1:30 | KABOOM mode (Marge explains it), power-ups, thin ice, snowbanks | Win · Break the ice under a Lumberjack · Trigger KABOOM |\n| 3 | **Gloves Off** | Grindhouse vs Bruise Brothers, 3 × 1:30, they challenge often | fights, the sin bin, power plays, hazards (octopi, rats), chirps | Win · Win 2 fights · Score a power-play goal |\n| 4 | **Mall Brawl** | MegaMall vs Megaplex Marauders, 3 × 1:30 with no OT, then a **Shootout Showcase** every time (it decides a tie; otherwise it is a bonus round for mall money and a toast) | the mascot, Discount Drop, the shootout and manual goalie | Win · Score a KABOOM goal · Knock down Polar Pete |\n| 5 | **The Kaboom Cup** | Kaboom Dome vs Gilded Grizzlies, 3 × 2:00, OT and shootout if tied | the boss: Sterling's Golden Twister, The Vault, Gilded Mode, Glitterman's Gilded Boost (Grizzlies +10% speed from the 3rd period), Doris's organ counter (Muskrats BOOM +30 and +10% speed for 20 s) | Win · Beat The Vault with a deke goal · One player scores a hat trick |\n\n**Script beats** (TEXT holds the full lines; these set the voice. Speakers in caps, choices in brackets):\n\n*Chapter 1 pre-game (locker room)*\n- MARGE: \"Sit down, shut up, and listen. I got a letter.\"\n- MARGE: \"Goldie Glitterman bought the land under the Icebox. Wants to pave it for a {c=#ffd36a}Megaplex Parking\n  Experience{/c}.\"\n- DUNNY: \"A parking… experience? Beauty. Wait. No. Not beauty.\"\n- SNIPES: \"This barn's got more character than his whole bank account. And his haircut.\"\n- MARGE: \"Bylaw 1897-B. Any rink that houses the Kaboom Cup stands forever. So we win the Cup.\"\n- LOU (knitting): \"Five games, then. Like the five petals of the wild rose.\"\n- LEMMY: \"Pipesy says we win. Clang's not so sure. Clang's a pessimist.\"\n- GLITTERMAN (in the doorway): \"Enjoy the barn, folks. I've ordered the parking meters. Gold ones.\"\n- MARGE: \"Captain. Tell 'em how we play tonight.\" [CLEAN AND FAST / MEAN AND LOUD]\n- DUNNY: \"We get pucks deep, we get bodies to the net, and we— uh— {$tacticLine}\"\n- MARGE: \"Warm-up's on. Then we drill the Drillers.\"\n\n*Chapter 1 post-game*: CHUCK: \"The Muskrats take the opener! The Icebox is ROCKIN'!\" · GLITTERMAN: \"Beginner's luck.\nThe meters are still on order.\" · MARGE: \"Pack your long johns. Lake Kabonk. Pond rules.\"\n\n*Chapter 2 pre-game (the lake at dusk, by the bonfire)*: BIG TIMBER: \"Welcome to the woods, Muskrats. We don't check.\nWe FELL.\" · SNIPES: \"Cute beard. Did you grow it, or did a beaver move in?\" · LEMMY: \"The ice is talking. It says\n'crack'.\" · MARGE: \"Thin ice is a tool. Hit 'em where it's thin.\" · MARGE: \"And listen. When the whole team's hummin'\n— hits, passes, the crowd losin' its mind — the ice starts to shake. That's a KABOOM. Fill the meter and let it\nrip.\" · LOU: \"Like thunder in a teacup.\" · [tactic choice]\n*Post*: BIG TIMBER: \"You hit like a falling spruce. Good on ya.\" · DUNNY: \"Thanks! You smell like one!\" · MARGE: \"Next\nstop, the Grindhouse. Bring a mouthguard. Bring two.\"\n\n*Chapter 3 pre-game (the Grindhouse's dim locker room)*: ROCCO: \"Well, well. Lou Beaudoin.\" · ROLLO: \"Lou 'The\nLibrary' Beaudoin.\" · ROCCO: \"Heard you knit now.\" · ROLLO: \"Heard you purl.\" · LOU: \"I have retired from fisticuffs,\ngentlemen.\" · MARGE: \"Retire after the game.\" · MARGE: \"In this barn they drop the gloves, you drop 'em back. Win the\nscrap, win the barn. Lose it, you sit in the sin bin and think about your choices.\" · [LET LOU LOOSE / KEEP IT ON THE\nICE]\n*Post*: ROLLO: \"He knitted me a scarf.\" · ROCCO: \"For my neck.\" · ROLLO: \"Which he bruised.\" · LOU: \"There is an ice pack\nin the pocket.\" · MARGE: \"Next, the Megaplex. Glitterman's turf. Watch your wallets.\"\n\n*Chapter 4 pre-game (rink-side under the neon)*: CHAD (filming himself): \"What's up, Mall Rats! Smash that glass,\nbro!\" · DUNNY: \"We're Muskrats.\" · CHAD: \"Same content, bro.\" · GLITTERMAN (to Lemmy): \"Name your price, goalie.\" ·\nLEMMY: \"…Pipesy says no. Clang says no with a curse word.\" · POLAR PETE: (a dance and a muffled babble) · MARGE:\n\"That bear's on the ice all game. Treat him like furniture.\" [IGNORE THE BEAR / HUNT THE BEAR] · MARGE: \"And win or\ntie, the mall's got a Shootout Showcase after. Mall money. We want it.\"\n*Post*: GLITTERMAN: \"Fine. The Final. My Grizzlies. My Dome. My rules.\" · SNIPES: \"Your Dome's gonna need a new roof.\"\n\n*Chapter 5 pre-game (the Dome's tunnel, then the spotlight intro)*: STERLING: \"I've never lost. Not once. Not even\nat Go Fish.\" · SNIPES: \"There's a first time for everything, Goldilocks.\" · THE VAULT: \"…\" · LEMMY: \"He's very big,\nPipesy.\" · MARGE: \"Forty-six years behind that bench. I've seen better teams. Prettier teams. Teams that could spell.\"\n· MARGE: \"Never saw one that wanted it more. Go make it go KABOOM.\" · [DORIS EARLY / DORIS LATE]\n*In-game*: when the Grizzlies' Gilded Boost starts, GLITTERMAN on the jumbotron: \"Synergy, boys!\" When Doris\nplays, MARGE: \"DORIS! PLAY THE SONG!\" (the organ's charge fanfare, the crowd claps, the boost).\n*Post (win), the ending*: the handshake line (both teams) → Dunny lifts the Kaboom Cup, which goes off in a confetti\nexplosion. CHUCK: \"THE KABOOM CUP IS… KA-BOOMING!\" → GLITTERMAN: \"My parking meters…\" → MARGE: \"Bylaw 1897-B, Goldie.\nLook it up.\" → GUS: \"Yep.\" → the Flood Wagon drives a lap with the team on top → **credits** over the run's highlight\nreplays (7.16), then Coach Marge: \"Same time next year.\" → the title, with the **Cup on display** in the Icebox from\nthen on.\n\n**Unlocks** (15 stars in all; exhibition cheats): 3★ Big Heads (`headR` × 1.8) · 6★ Octopus Rain · 9★ Glow Puck · 12★\nAlways KABOOM (for humans) · 15★ Retro Rigs (`style: 'classic'`). Finishing the story makes the Gilded Grizzlies and\nThe Vault playable in exhibition and adds the Cup to the title screen.\n\n### 11.4 Practice: Coach Marge's Drills (at the Ol' Icebox, house lights half on)\n| # | Drill | Pass condition | Teaches |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Wheels | skate through 6 gates in order in 25 s (one gate wants a hockey stop) | skating, turbo, stops |\n| 2 | Tape to Tape | 5 completed passes to moving teammates + 1 saucer over a sled | passes, saucers, aim |\n| 3 | Top Shelf | hit 4 corner targets on an empty net (wrist and slap) | shots, aim, lift |\n| 4 | One-Timers | 3 one-timer goals on Lemmy from Dunny's cross-crease feeds | one-timers |\n| 5 | Finish Your Check | big-hit 3 training dummies into the glass and break a panel | checks, turbo hits, glass |\n| 6 | Gloves Off | win a spar with Big Lou (he goes easy) | the fight controls |\n| 7 | KABOOM! | with a full meter, score with a KABOOM shot and survive Lou's KABOOM check | KABOOM mode |\n\nEach drill opens with a Marge line (voiced) and a prompt panel with glyph chips, tracks its counter in the HUD, and\nsaves its completion. Completing all 7 earns the \"Marge Approved\" badge (Records). Chapter 1 offers drills 1–3 as\nits warm-up.\n\n### 11.5 Text pools (in `07-data-text.js`; sizes are the minimums)\nCommentary: 18 event types × 4–8 lines (≈ 110 lines) plus 20 Moose filler anecdotes; chirps: 30; tips: 14;\nthree-stars lines: 12; loss pep talks: 5; menu blurbs: 1 per item; About pages (12.1). Appendix D has samples for each.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Screens and flows (10-foot UI)\n\n**Rules for every screen**: at most 6 choices visible; big tiles and cards; one line of help; a legend at the bottom\nwith glyph chips (`{pass} SELECT  {deke} BACK`, as keycaps or mouse icons for keyboard and mouse). D-pad, stick,\narrows and WASD move focus; ✕ / Enter / Space pick; ○ / Esc / Backspace go back. **The mouse hovering a tile focuses\nit and a click picks it.** Focus has an animated gold border, a slight scale-up and an organ blip. No dense tables\nanywhere: stats are a few big numbers.\n\n1. **Title**: the Ol' Icebox at night, spotlights sweeping the ice, two teams skating lazily (AI). The logo slams in\n   with an explosion and the horn, then `PRESS ANY BUTTON` (`TAP` is never shown; see 15.2). Then the main menu: 6 tiles\n   in 2 rows: **CUP RUN** (Continue/New when a save exists), **EXHIBITION**, **PRACTICE**, **RECORDS**, **SETTINGS**\n   (the engine's settings screen: `game.menu('settings')`), **ABOUT**. The version label (`E.versionLabel()` + the\n   game's version) sits small in a corner, and the engine corner buttons stay at the top right.\n2. **Exhibition → Sides**: every joined player is a token in the middle column (CPU); push left or right to join HOME\n   or AWAY; ✕ to ready. \"Press START on a free controller, or 2 on the keyboard, to join\" (`game.allowJoin({ max: 4\n   })`). The keyboard halves show their keys. Mouse: click HOME or AWAY to move the keyboard player's token.\n3. **Exhibition → Setup**: 3 big cards side by side: HOME team, ARENA, AWAY team (left/right on a focused card cycles\n   it; each team card shows its logo ×3, name, and 4 pip bars: Speed, Shooting, Hitting, Goalie). Below, one row of\n   option chips: Periods (1/2/3), Period length (1:00 / 1:30 / 2:00 / 3:00 / 4:00), Difficulty, Cheats (unlocked\n   ones). **FACE OFF!** starts.\n4. **Story map**: the bus on a snowy highway with 5 stops (each a town sign with its logo and earned stars). The stop\n   in focus shows the chapter title and objectives. Click a stop to pick it.\n5. **Cutscene**: the set (the locker room or rink-side), characters staged, `E.Dialog` boxes with live portraits,\n   babble and typed text; choices are 2 big options. ✕ advances; holding ○ for 1 s skips the scene (with a fill ring).\n6. **Pre-game card**: matchup logos, the arena, the objectives with ★ slots, the tactic chosen. ✕ FACE OFF.\n7. **Match** (HUD 7.18). **Pause** (engine): Resume, Objectives & Info (the story objectives, or the exhibition's\n   setup), Restart Game, **Dev Mode**, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title.\n8. **Intermission**: the period summary card (goals, shots, hits: big numbers), then `{pass} DRIVE THE FLOOD WAGON`\n   or `{deke} SKIP`.\n9. **Results**: the final score huge, the **three stars** revealed one by one (portrait cards, a stat line, a\n   commentary line), the objectives ticking ★, then CONTINUE / REMATCH / MAIN MENU.\n10. **Records**: big numbers with a label each: Hardest Shot (km/h = u/s ÷ 16 × 3.6), Biggest Hit, Most Goals in a\n    Game, Fights Won, KABOOMs, Story Stars x/15, Drills x/7. Two pages at most.\n11. **About**: section 12.1's pages, paged with L1/R1, left/right or a click on the arrows.\n12. **Credits**: the end roll over highlight replays.\n\n### 12.1 About / Credits screen\nPages (at most 8 lines each, in the large font): **Credits** (game design and code: Claude Opus 5.5, `claude-opus-5-5`,\nfor Michael Crosato's cc-matrix; engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2, MIT; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; every sound, voice and\nsong synthesized in code; asset-store props from CC0 sets, listed by name) · **Source Information** (every field TASK.md\nlists) · **Testing Feedback** · **Engine Feedback** · **Prompt Feedback** · **Engine changes** (the summary of\nENGINE-CHANGES.md). The builder fills the feedback pages at the end with the same text as the chat reply and\n`exit-interview.json`, writing \"unknown\" for anything that can't be confirmed.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Settings (via `menu.settings`; the engine's Display, Sound, Comfort and Controls stay)\nButton symbols (PlayStation / Xbox) · Difficulty (Rookie / Pro / All-Star / Legend) · Period length (exhibition default)\n· Camera (Broadcast / Overhead) · Camera distance (Near / Normal / Far) · Commentary (On / Off) · Subtitles (On / Off) ·\nVoices volume · Crowd volume · Player intros (On / Off) · Replays (Auto / Off) · Flood Wagon (Ask / Always / Never) ·\nPuck trail (Off / Streak / Glow) · Tips (On / Off) · Reset tips. Every one is read live.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Online: AI Hub sessions (`Net`, shared-world)\n\n### 14.1 Page tags (in `<head>`, after the session client)\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Outscore the other team in one 3-minute period\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD skate · ✕/J pass · □/K shoot · ○/L deke · R2/Shift turbo\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n```\n\n### 14.2 Flow (when `AIHub.active`)\n1. There is no title, attract or menu. Boot first calls\n   `info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If `info` is null, carry on\n   exactly as outside a session. Otherwise it picks the teams and the arena (step 2), builds the arena, and calls\n   `AIHub.ready()` (step 4).\n2. **Teams**: even seats (0, 2) are HOME and odd seats (1, 3) AWAY; with one player, that player is HOME vs the CPU.\n   The two teams and the arena are picked by `AIHub.rng('setup')`, the same on every copy; the host's first snapshot\n   confirms them. The CPU fills the rest. In a 2v1, the lone human's CPU teammates get AI skill +.15.\n3. **Our own card** (scene `session`, until `start`): the arena at night with spotlights; each player's skater lined\n   up on their team's blue line with a nameplate in their seat color (names sanitized for the pixel font, drawn on\n   the canvas, never put into HTML); \"HOW TO WIN: Outscore the other team in one 3-minute period\"; THIS PLAYER'S\n   CONTROLS as glyph chips for their device; a ✓ on each ready player; the countdown from the `card` event. Enter or\n   ✕ (button 0), or a click or tap on READY, calls `AIHub.answer('ready')`. △ (button 3), T, or a click on MORE TIME\n   calls `AIHub.answer('more')` (pressing again takes it back). The card changes nothing in the round.\n4. Call `AIHub.ready()` once the arena is built, with no key press.\n5. On `start`, show a big 3–2–1 while `AIHub.time() < 0`, then a faceoff at time 0. The match config is 1 period of\n   3:00, then sudden-death OT capped at 1:00, then a tie. Replays are 3 s, there are no intros and no Flood Wagon;\n   fights and items are on.\n6. **The host** (`info.isHost`) runs `Match.step` with all CPU AI and the remote players' intents. It calls\n   `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` exactly once: at the final horn, on `time-up` (at once, with\n   the current score), or when a round that began with 2+ players is down to one human (`leave`; the leavers are left\n   out of the standings). Standings list the winning team's remaining players in one array and the losers in the\n   next; a tie puts everyone in one array. With 1 player,\n   `standings: [[id]]` and `won: true | false`. `scores` maps each id to their own points (goals + assists); `stats`\n   maps each id to `{ Goals, Assists, Hits, Fights }`; `awards` are the three stars that are humans\n   (`{ id, title: '1st Star', detail }`).\n7. **Leaving**: a human who leaves becomes a CPU skater. The hub voids the round when the host leaves.\n8. On `end`: stop input and sound (`audio.music(null)`, mute), freeze on the final score, and send nothing more.\n9. **No pausing in a session**: the gameplay scene is not `pausable` and `autoPause` is off. Options (or Esc) opens a\n   small non-pausing overlay (Sound, Music, Voices, Button symbols, Camera, Back), during which the local skater\n   coasts. There is no Quit, Restart or Dev Mode. Create + Options belongs to the hub (engine patch 2). Use no\n   `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt` or `window.open`, and no network but the hub.\n10. **Server copies** (`info.server`: the host with no player): they run the same host code with no local input or\n    camera and draw only a small \"HOSTING\" line.\n\n### 14.3 Netcode (it stays within 20 messages a second per copy and 16 KB per message)\n- **Clients → host**, 15 Hz, unreliable, `{ t: 'in', s: seq, at: AIHub.time() rounded, mx, my (×100 rounded),\n  h: bits (shoot, lob, turbo), c: [pass, shoot, deke, lob, chirp, switch] press counters (mod 256), ax, ay (aim, or\n  omitted) }`. The host turns counter differences into presses, so a lost packet loses no taps, and treats the\n  latest packet as held state. The host acknowledges with `ack` per player.\n- **Host → all**, 15 Hz, unreliable, under 1,200 bytes: `{ t: 's', n: tick, at, ph: phase code, p: period,\n  k: clock ×10, sc: [h, a], b: [boomH, boomA, kaboomFlags], pk: [x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, owner], e: [[id, x, y, vx, vy,\n  facing (0–255), state code, stateT ×10, flags], × 8 (6 skaters + 2 goalies)], ack: { playerId: seq }, it: items,\n  f: fight state (when fighting), ev: [recent events with ids, each repeated in 4 snapshots] }`. Integers only.\n- **Reliable host messages** (rare): `setup` (teams, arena, seat → skater map), `phase` changes (goal, period end,\n  final, fight start and end), and `glass` and `hole` state changes.\n- **Clients render** others interpolated about 120 ms behind the newest snapshot (two snapshot intervals less a\n  margin; tune it with the harness's latency and jitter settings). **Their own skater is predicted**: it\n  starts from the snapshot's authoritative state at `ack`, re-applies the pending intents with `Skater.skateStep`\n  (ignoring collisions), and blends the drawn position toward the result over 0.1 s, snapping when off by more than\n  48. While the client's skater owns the puck, the puck is drawn at its predicted blade. Each client plays effects,\n  sounds and commentary from the snapshot events it receives (deduplicated by id); the host sends commentary line ids\n  inside the events. Instant replays run on each copy from its own snapshot history.\n- **Budget**: the host sends 15 snapshots a second plus a few reliable messages, so it stays under 20/s. Each client\n  sends 15 inputs a second plus rare reliable messages.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Attract mode, touch-only devices and dev mode\n\n### 15.1 Attract mode (scene `attract`)\n- **Idle timer** on title, menus, side select, setup, the story map, records and about: 10 s without any input (keys,\n  buttons, clicks, wheel, a mouse move of more than 8 px, a stick or trigger past .3) → `game.go('attract', null,\n  { fade: 'dissolve' })`. Not during cutscenes, matches or the engine's open menus, and never in sessions.\n- **The reel**: a script (`game.script`) of segments, each built on the real match simulation with every skater on\n  AI, cheats free (infinite turbo, forced events, warping the puck or players). Each loop picks a new arena and teams.\n  1. *Puck Drop* (8 s): the intro spotlights, a faceoff, play.\n  2. *Big Hits* (8 s): a forced turbo big hit into the glass, which shatters.\n  3. *Highlight Goal* (12 s): a set-up 2-on-1, a cross-crease pass, a one-timer goal, the horn and the instant replay.\n  4. *Gloves Off* (10 s): an AI-vs-AI fight to a knockdown.\n  5. *KABOOM!* (10 s): forced KABOOM mode, a KABOOM shot that blasts the goalie into the net.\n  6. *Fan Frenzy* (7 s): items thrown and grabbed; an octopus slip.\n  7. *Story teaser* (8 s): 3 cutscene lines with portraits and babble.\n  8. *Flood Wagon* (6 s): the AI driver resurfacing scuffed ice.\n  9. *Records card* (5 s): the logo, `PRESS ANY BUTTON`, and the top records.\n  The loop is about 75 s, then it starts again.\n- **Overlay**: a `DEMO` tag, the logo bug, and `PRESS ANY BUTTON` (glyph per device) blinking. On touch-only devices\n  it reads \"Controller or keyboard required\" instead.\n- **Any input** ends it: back to the title with that input consumed (`input.consumeAll()`), so it triggers nothing\n  else. The audio follows the settings (browsers stay silent until a first gesture anyway).\n\n### 15.2 Touch-only devices\n- **Detection**: `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches`, no gamepad\n  seen, and no key pressed since load. Re-check on `gamepadconnected` and the first `keydown`; either one switches to\n  normal at once.\n- **Touch-only**: no touch controls anywhere (`touch: []` on every scene, the engine's touch buttons hidden). The title\n  shows a large banner, \"Controller or keyboard required\", and a big **SETTINGS** button (a tap opens\n  `game.menu('settings')`); the engine's corner menu button stays. Taps don't start the game. The attract mode runs by\n  the same 10 s rule, and taps don't leave it (only to open Settings).\n\n### 15.3 Dev mode (scene overlay `Dev`, from the pause menu's **Dev Mode** item; also `#dev`)\n- Choosing it closes the engine's pause menu and opens the Dev panel. While the panel is open the match holds its own\n  `devPause` flag (the engine's `game.paused` is false, so the panel can read input), unless **Live** is toggled on: the panel docks to the right at 45% width and the game runs behind it, so slider\n  changes show at once.\n- **Navigation**: L1/R1 (or Tab, or a click) switch tabs; up/down move; left/right adjust (hold to accelerate; L2/R2\n  ×10 steps); △ (or R) resets the row; **RESET ALL TO DEFAULTS** is the first row of TUNING; ○ / Esc closes. The mouse\n  hovers to focus rows, drags sliders and clicks toggles. Each row shows its value and its default.\n- **TUNING** tab: every `T` key with a slider (Appendix A), grouped Skating, Puck & Passing, Shooting, Goalies,\n  Hitting, AI, BOOM & Items, Fights, Match. Values persist in `E.store('dev:tuning')`. **Log tuning** prints a JSON of\n  the non-default values to the console, for designers.\n- **CHEATS**: infinite turbo; god mode (no knockdowns); always KABOOM; puck magnet (the puck comes to the human's\n  blade); freeze AI; CPU goalies off; big heads; octopus rain; glow puck; retro rigs; instant BOOM full (an action).\n- **WARP**: start any chapter or cutscene; jump to period 2, 3 or OT, or the shootout; set the clock to 0:10; score\n  +1 for home or away; win or lose this game now; spawn each item or hazard at center; start a fight; start KABOOM;\n  break the thin ice; shatter a panel; trigger the Flood Wagon; go to results, attract, about or the lab.\n- **DEBUG**: overlays (bodies and radii, blade points, AI roles and targets, the puck's predicted path, goalie save\n  shapes, grudge numbers, rig skeletons via `rig.debug(r)`), FPS, slow motion (1, .5, .25), frame step (paused: ✕\n  advances one step), free camera (the stick pans, the triggers zoom), hide the HUD (screenshot mode), the RNG seed,\n  and a **sound test** (play every sfx, song, layer, organ sting and voice, including a babble line per character).\n- **Not available in AI Hub sessions.**\n\n---\n\n## 16. Build order and milestones\nBuild in this order. Each milestone ends with its tests passing (`node tests/run.mjs`) and a look at its screenshots.\nThe game must be playable from M3 on.\n\n| M | Deliverable | Acceptance |\n|---|---|---|\n| **M0 Setup** | dev folder, the engine copied, the vendor files, `tools/build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` running an empty suite, `src/` skeleton, a title scene that boots in the browser and headless, ENGINE-CHANGES.md started | the built HTML opens from `file://` with no errors (`tools/check.mjs`); the headless boot test passes |\n| **M1 Rink, skating, rigs** | `Rink` geometry and drawing (ice, lines, boards, glass panels, nets, benches), the floor TileMap, `skateStep`, SkaterRig (stride, glide, stop, crossovers, stick idle), the broadcast camera, the animation lab | unit tests for geometry and skating; filmstrips of stride and stop look right; screenshots of the Icebox rink in all 3 views |\n| **M2 Puck play** | the puck, possession, stick-handling, passes (lead, saucer), one-timers, wrist and slap shots, goal detection, posts, net bulge, Goalie v1 (positioning, save solver, rebounds, freeze), HOCKEY_KEYS, mouse and right-stick aim, glyph chips, font patch, HUD v1 | headless: a pass reaches a stationary and a moving mate; a shot into an empty net scores; a shot at the goalie is saved; a post hit emits `post`; glyph labels per device |\n| **M3 First playable match** | Match flow (faceoffs, clock, stoppages, goals, celebrations, periods, final, results, three stars), team AI, the referee, the crowd v1, audio v1 (sfx, the horn, the organ, the crowd bed, the theme), Exhibition Setup (1 player) | AI vs AI plays 3 periods with no errors and 3–12 goals; a bot-driven human match (the bot of 18.3) completes; `balance.mjs` runs |\n| **M4 Over the top** | checks, knockdowns, the glass, turbo, deke, poke, BOOM and KABOOM, items and hazards, chirps, commentary with babble voices, instant replay, Fx | headless: the big-hit threshold, glass crack then shatter, KABOOM start, shot and end, item effects, replay playback ends and returns to a faceoff |\n| **M5 Fights, OT, multiplayer, menus** | fights and the sin bin, OT and the shootout (manual goalie), local 1–4 players and side select, all 10-foot menus, settings, records, about | headless: a fight from gloves to a winner and the sin bin timer; a shootout to a decision; 4 inputs each moving their own skater; mouse hover focus and click in menus (browser) |\n| **M6 Story and content** | all 5 arenas dressed (lights, props, crowds, hazards), all 6 teams, the story map, the cutscene runner and every script, choices, objectives, stars and unlocks, the Flood Wagon minigame, the 7 practice drills, the boss (The Vault, Golden Twister, Gilded Mode, Boost and organ), the ending and credits with highlights, saves | the whole-story playthrough test passes (18.3); screenshots of every arena and every cutscene set |\n| **M7 Attract, touch, dev** | the attract reel, idle detection, touch-only mode, the Dev panel (all 4 tabs), the sound test | headless: idle 10 s → attract; all 9 segments visited; any input → title; dev slider change and reset; browser: a touch-only emulation shows the banner and attract runs |\n| **M8 AI Hub** | `Net` (connect, card, host and client, prediction, events, finish), the metas, session flow | the fake-hub headless test (18.5) passes; the real harness passes in all 4 configurations (18.6) |\n| **M9 Polish and balance** | tuning passes with `balance.mjs`, act on `check.mjs` look notes, every screenshot reviewed at 1280×720 and 1920×1080, the About pages and `exit-interview.json` filled in, the final build | the full `node tests/run.mjs` is green; no TODO or placeholder strings; `exit-interview.json` parses; the HTML runs from `file://` with no network requests |\n\n---\n\n## 17. Risks and how to de-risk them\n| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| Skater and stick animation | new motion on a procedural rig decides whether it reads as hockey | built first (M1) in the animation lab; filmstrip every motion; keep solvePose overrides small and data-driven; fall back to the engine's poses for rare states |\n| Puck feel (possession, passes, one-timers) | the core of the fun; easy to get floaty or sticky | every constant a slider from day one; headless pass and shot tests; play it at M2 before building on it |\n| Goalie believability | too good is frustrating, too weak is boring | a physical save solver (reaction, lateral speed, shapes) rather than dice; `balance.mjs` shoots 200 shots per type and checks the save-rate bands in 7.6 |\n| Curved boards, glass and depth sorting | custom drawing in a tile engine | far boards as background, end and corner panels queued per panel, near boards cut low; screenshots in all views at M1 |\n| Netcode under latency, loss and limits | shared world, 20 msgs/s, unreliable packets | a pure `skateStep` for prediction; press counters; snapshots under 1,200 bytes (a test asserts it); a fake hub in Node with latency and loss before the real harness |\n| Hub compliance | a session fails the harness's checklist | follow 14.2 step by step; the harness at M8 in all 4 configurations; no pause, quit or dialogs in sessions |\n| Audio quality (babble, horn, organ) | voices can sound like noise | the sound test in Dev from M4; tune formants by ear; keep the voice bus quieter than the sfx bus |\n| PlayStation glyphs in the pixel font | they rendered as `?` | the font patch plus glyph chips at M2; a test renders each chip |\n| Scope | a big demo | milestones in value order; data-driven content; the systems shared by story, drills, attract and sessions (all are `Match` configs) |\n| Determinism (replays, tests, attract) | hidden `Math.random` use | only `RNG.sim` in the simulation; a test runs the same seed twice and compares a state hash |\n\n---\n\n## 18. Testing\n\n**One command**: `node tests/run.mjs` builds, then runs every suite in order and prints **only failures** plus one\nline: `ICE HOC-KABOOM TESTS: 214 passed, 0 failed (headless 9 suites, browser 3, hub 4) in 182 s`.\n`--quick` runs only the headless suites; `--only <suite>` reruns one (after changing the code it covers). Headless\nsuites load `build/game.js` into a `vm` context with the stand-ins from `engine/kits/test.mjs` (`window`,\n`addEventListener`, `location`). They drive the game with `game.advance`, `input.tap` and `input.hold`, and read\n`game.debug.snapshot()`. No subagents or workflows review anything; the scripts decide.\n\n### 18.1 Unit (pure functions)\nRink inside, normal and clamp at corners; the faceoff dot table; `skateStep` (time to top speed, stop distance, turn\nradius at speed, turbo drain); puck friction distance; board reflection angles; post ping; goal-line crossing (inside\nvs post); pass lead hits a moving mate; shot aim stays inside the mouth for σ = 0; save-shape tests; impulse\nthresholds; BOOM gain table; fight damage and stamina; tuning reset and resetAll; the glyph label per device and\nsetting; the name sanitizer; snapshot encode, decode and size (< 1,200 bytes for 8 entities, 3 items and 4 events);\ninput packet press counters across a dropped packet; objective predicates.\n\n### 18.2 Systems (headless game)\n- A faceoff leads to possession within 2 s.\n- A scripted wrist shot from the slot at an empty net scores.\n- A slapshot at the goalie from the blue line is saved.\n- A one-timer cross-crease scores at least 4 of 10 seeded tries.\n- A turbo check at full speed knocks down; a second hit into the same panel shatters it, and the puck leaves through\n  it → a faceoff.\n- Holding △ near a rival with a grudge starts a fight; scripted jabs win it; the loser is in the sin bin for 20 s; a\n  power-play banner shows.\n- Filling BOOM starts KABOOM; a KABOOM shot blasts the goalie; it ends after 15 s.\n- Each item applies its effect and expires; thin ice breaks after a big hit; a skater in a hole is frozen 3 s.\n- The period ends at 0:00 → intermission → the next period; OT is sudden death; the shootout reaches a decision.\n- Results show three stars.\n- 4 local players each move only their own skater.\n- Replay plays and returns.\n- The same seed and inputs twice give the same state hash after 60 s (determinism).\n\n### 18.3 Scripted playthrough of the whole game (`tests/play-story.mjs`)\nFrom boot: title → CUP RUN → for chapters 1 to 5: advance the cutscene (tap confirm; take choice 1 in chapters 1, 3\nand 5, choice 2 in 2 and 4), run warm-up drills 1–3 in chapter 1 by script, then play the match with **the bot\ncontrolling the human team's skater through `game.input`** (the CPU intent turned into stick and buttons, as in the\nSPORTS kit's `bot()`), with dev tuning giving the home team AI skill .95 and the rivals .3 so each game is won in real\nplay. Play 1 period for real, then warp the clock to 0:05 for the remaining periods, keeping the lead. Play the\nintermission Flood Wagon once with the bot steering, the chapter 4 Shootout Showcase, and the chapter 5 boss phases\n(the Boost and organ events must fire). Then the post-game, results, the map, the ending, credits and back to the\ntitle. Assert at each stage: the expected scene and chapter, at least one goal per game, no errors, stars recorded,\nthe save written, and every chapter's new mechanic event seen (one-timer, kaboom_start, thin_ice_break, fight_end,\nmascot_down, shootout_end, vault_cracked or a boss goal). If real play hasn't produced a chapter's signature event by\nthe end of its first period, trigger it with the Dev warp (`game.debug.warp('breakIce')` and the like), then assert\nthat the game handled it (its consequences, commentary and objective). Also play **Practice drills 1–7** by script and\nassert each passes.\n\n### 18.4 Other headless suites\n- **Attract**: idle 10 s from the title → attract; run 80 s; all 9 segments visited; tapping confirm → title with\n  the input consumed.\n- **Dev**: open from the pause menu item; change 3 sliders (the values apply to the match); reset one; reset all\n  (all defaults); a cheat toggles; warps work.\n- **Exhibition**: 60 s with 4 players, each scheme.\n- **Balance** (`balance.mjs`; it also prints a table when run alone): 20 AI-vs-AI games at Pro, averaging 5–10 goals\n  a game; save % .78–.90; at least 2 fights per 10 games; KABOOM 1–4 per game; plus 7.6's shot-type bands.\n- **Text**: every TEXT pool meets its minimum; every `{token}` resolves; no line wider than its box at scale 1.\n\n### 18.5 Fake-hub network test (headless, Node)\nTwo to four `vm` contexts, each with the engine, the game and a fake `AIHub` (an in-memory bus with configurable\nlatency 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss). It runs connect → card (scripted ready) → start → 60 s of scripted play → time-up.\nAssert: the host's and clients' scores match; a client's own-skater error stays below 12 u on average; presses are\nnever lost; `finish` is called once with valid standings; a leaving client's skater turns CPU; a server-mode host\nworks.\n\n### 18.6 Browser suites (Playwright 1.63, Chromium; `TMPDIR` set)\n- `engine/tools/check.mjs` on the built HTML and on `#match/muskrats/drillers/icebox`, `#fight` and `#kaboom`: no\n  errors, and every look note handled.\n- **Menus and input**: keyboard navigation through the main menu; mouse hover moves focus and a click picks;\n  `lastDevice` changes switch the prompt chips; Settings → Xbox changes the chips.\n- **Touch-only**: `--size 390x844@3` with coarse-pointer emulation shows the banner and SETTINGS, and attract starts\n  after 10 s.\n- **Hub harness**: serve `dev/hub/` (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, confirm the page title, kill by\n  PID afterwards). Open `harness.html?game=game.html&players=2&auto=1`; then\n  `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; then the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; then\n  `&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Each waits for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and asserts\n  `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, printing the failed checks otherwise. Then the game outside a session still\n  reaches the title.\n\n### 18.7 Screenshots (only for what scripts can't judge; `tests/shots.mjs`)\nAt 1280×720 and 1920×1080: title, the attract segments, side select with 4 players, setup, every arena at a faceoff,\na big hit and shattered glass, a fight, KABOOM mode, a goal celebration, a replay, results with three stars, a\ncutscene with a portrait, the story map, a drill, the Flood Wagon, the Dev panel, Settings with Xbox glyphs, the\nAbout pages, the session card (from the harness), and the touch-only banner at 390×844. Look at every one, comparing\nagainst the look target (8) and the 10-foot rules (12).\n\n---\n\n## 19. Definition of done (TASK.md → where it is met)\n- [ ] Genre and perspective chosen and used (0, 7.15). Title from a real RNG (0).\n- [ ] Single HTML with the given name, the dev folder, no network requests (1).\n- [ ] Built on the handoff engine; changes logged (4) and summarized in About.\n- [ ] Native look with new hockey art (8); native animation with new hockey motion (9).\n- [ ] All audio in code; gibberish voices (10).\n- [ ] AI Hub sessions passing the harness, plus local multiplayer for the game on its own (14, 6.1, 12).\n- [ ] Feature-complete demo: story, exhibition, practice, records and every mechanic shown in play, drills and attract\n      (11, 12, 15.1).\n- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu with live sliders and reset to defaults (15.3).\n- [ ] Attract mode after 10 s idle on title and menus; any input exits (15.1).\n- [ ] 10-foot, controller-first UI; native keyboard and mouse (aim, hover focus, click); prompts follow the last\n      device; PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option (6, 12).\n- [ ] Touch-only: \"Controller or keyboard required\", the settings button, attract runs (15.2).\n- [ ] Narrative tone: hockey broadcast and small-town hockey comedy (11.3, Appendix D).\n- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubs (a test enforces it).\n- [ ] Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in the chat reply **and** the About\n      screen; `exit-interview.json` in TASK.md's exact shape, parsing as JSON. Suggested `aiHub` values: name\n      \"Ice Hoc-Kaboom\"; tagline \"Over-the-top 3-on-3 arcade hockey\"; description \"Glass-shattering hits, dropped\n      gloves and explosive KABOOM slapshots as the Mukluk Falls Muskrats fight to save their rink. Story, exhibition\n      and up to four players.\"; type \"Game\"; genre \"Sports\"; source \"Ice hockey\"; series \"\"; players \"1–4\"; controls\n      \"Stick/WASD skate · ✕/J pass · □/K shoot · ○/L deke · △/I saucer & gloves · R2/Shift turbo\"; tags\n      `[\"arcade\", \"sports\", \"versus\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\", \"story\"]`. The Source Information `plan` field is\n      `PLAN.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: Tuning defaults (`T`; every row is a Dev slider)\n| Group | Key | Default | Min–max | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Skating | skateMax | 132 | 80–200 | top speed (u/s) at rating 3 |\n| | skateAccel | 300 | 120–600 | acceleration |\n| | iceGlide | 28 | 0–120 | coasting deceleration |\n| | turnSlow / turnFast | 5.0 / 2.6 | 1–10 | rad/s at low and top speed |\n| | edgeGrip | 6 | 1–20 | sideways decay /s |\n| | stopDecel | 700 | 300–1400 | hockey-stop deceleration |\n| | turboMul | 1.45 | 1–2 | turbo speed factor |\n| | turboDrain / turboRegen | 0.45 / 0.18 | 0–2 | meter per second |\n| Puck & passing | puckFriction / puckDrag | 26 / 0.12 | 0–80 / 0–.5 | puck deceleration |\n| | boardBounce | 0.62 | .2–1 | boards restitution |\n| | pickupRadius | 8 | 4–16 | blade pickup |\n| | passMin / passMax | 240 / 420 | 150–600 | pass speeds |\n| | saucerApex | 10 | 4–24 | saucer height |\n| Shooting | wristSpeed | 330 | 200–500 | wrist shot |","numLines":450,"startLine":900,"totalLines":1473}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ux91F44i72kLjmKDpPDt32","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
