{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0194B2LhKgeWBwiEjPYB2Lb5","type":"tool_result","content":"197:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n202:- `px.ell(g, cx, cy, rx, ry, c)`: a filled ellipse\n244:- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)\n366:- `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity = 1, o)` †: radius in world units; intensity ~0.5..1.5. opts: { color: '#ffaa55' (both lightings), shadow: true (GPU lighting: walls and casters block it) }\n381:- `game.lights.tint = .32` †: how strongly lights add their own color, 0..1\n387:- `game.particles.bits(x, y, z, n, colors)`: n pieces of debris that fly, fall and bounce (colors: a list to pick from)\n389:- `game.particles.dust(x, y, z, n, o = {})`: n puffs of dust from (x, y, z) that drift and fade. o: { speed: 30, color, size }\n418:- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n419:- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n421:- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n423:- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n429:- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\n439:- `r.visible(x, y, z = 0, mx = 60, up = 30, down = 90)`: is a world point near the visible area? margins in pixels (characters extend upward from their feet)\n479:- `game.focus(x, y, z = 0)`: camera follows this world point. Side-scrollers: game.focus(x, 0, z)\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n498:- `game.setZoom(z)` †: camera zoom on top of the view: game.setZoom(1.5) (.5 .. 3), the game's own; where the scene lets the player zoom (camera.zoom), theirs multiplies it (game.zoom is the two together). Characters, maps, props, particles and lights are \n531:- `game.lights` †: canvas lighting (lights.enabled, lights.add in draw)\n558:- `game.zoom = 1` †: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de63938e-b4cc-4b63-8e8c-4cc91a6c7b2f","uuid":"d8f25e0b-9536-496e-bf0d-2cf69df3e520","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:08:45.008Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"197:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n202:- `px.ell(g, cx, cy, rx, ry, c)`: a filled ellipse\n244:- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)\n366:- `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity = 1, o)` †: radius in world units; intensity ~0.5..1.5. opts: { color: '#ffaa55' (both lightings), shadow: true (GPU lighting: walls and casters block it) }\n381:- `game.lights.tint = .32` †: how strongly lights add their own color, 0..1\n387:- `game.particles.bits(x, y, z, n, colors)`: n pieces of debris that fly, fall and bounce (colors: a list to pick from)\n389:- `game.particles.dust(x, y, z, n, o = {})`: n puffs of dust from (x, y, z) that drift and fade. o: { speed: 30, color, size }\n418:- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n419:- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n421:- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n423:- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n429:- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\n439:- `r.visible(x, y, z = 0, mx = 60, up = 30, down = 90)`: is a world point near the visible area? margins in pixels (characters extend upward from their feet)\n479:- `game.focus(x, y, z = 0)`: camera follows this world point. Side-scrollers: game.focus(x, 0, z)\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n498:- `game.setZoom(z)` †: camera zoom on top of the view: game.setZoom(1.5) (.5 .. 3), the game's own; where the scene lets the player zoom (camera.zoom), theirs multiplies it (game.zoom is the two together). Characters, maps, props, particles and lights are \n531:- `game.lights` †: canvas lighting 