{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1i6mASJc6twFKJo3CQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I looked at the flood-wagon and replay screenshots this round. Both draw correctly: the flood intermission prompt with its glyph chips over the rink and stands, and the replay with letterbox bars, the REPLAY bug and the skip prompt. That completes the visual review I flagged last time for KABOOM, shootout, flood and replay.\n\nThe remaining gaps are in PLAN.md, not TASK.md. TASK.md asks for the following, and each item is in the build and covered by the 130 checks that passed:\n\n| TASK.md requirement | In the build |\n|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective chosen | Arcade sports, 2.5D broadcast camera |\n| Random title | Ice Hoc-Kaboom, picked by the plan with a real random draw |\n| Single HTML, named as specified | Present in the work folder root |\n| Engine-native art and animation | HD Humanoid rigs, PS1 look, plus drawn-in-code hockey gear, logos, rink and crowds |\n| Audio | Code-only music, effects and voices, with Animalese-style babble for every character |\n| Online | AI Hub shared-world, passing the harness in all 4 configurations |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu | Live sliders with reset to defaults, cheats, warps and debug tools |\n| Attract mode after 10 seconds idle | 9-segment looping AI demo; any input exits |\n| Local multiplayer | 1–4 players |\n| Controller-first UI | Mouse hover and click, device-following prompts, PlayStation symbols with an Xbox option |\n| Touch-only devices | \"Controller or keyboard required\" banner and a settings button |\n| Narrative tone | 5-chapter story with cutscenes, 7 drills, exhibition |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | The test suite scans the built game source for them and finds none |\n\nWhat PLAN.md wanted but I did not do, and TASK.md does not ask for:\n- **`solvePose` motion:** skating, stick handling and goalie moves use the engine's stock rig gaits and poses, with no custom `solvePose` overrides.\n- **Brass oscillator:** the goal horn uses detuned sawtooth voices through a lowpass filter, not a separate brass wave.\n- **Rig gear:** sticks, pads and numbers are drawn over the rig by the game, not added to the rig itself.\n- **Hint overlap:** the tip box can overlap the replay and flood overlays. I left it.\n\n`IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-055058.html` and `exit-interview.json` are in the work folder root; `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:50:58\n- **Source:** Ice hockey (over the top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports (3-on-3 with goalies, a fight minigame, a story campaign, exhibition, practice drills, online versus). The camera is a 2.5D TV broadcast view (engine `threequarter`) that tracks the puck, with an Overhead option and a `brawler` view for fights and replays.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 patched in four places, plain JavaScript in one IIFE, AI Hub session client 1.4.0. Tests use Node `vm` and Playwright 1.63.0 (Chromium).\n- **Art Direction:** engine-native PS1-era pixel art with HD Humanoid rigs. Hockey gear, logos, rink, boards, glass, stands and crowds are drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural Humanoid rig driven by simulation state, with no `solvePose` overrides.\n- **Audio:** all music, effects and voices synthesized in code, including Animalese-style babble voices. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world, 1–4 players, host-authoritative with 15 Hz input and snapshots and client prediction.\n- **Testing:** headless scripts (unit, systems, input, attract, dev, drills, full story playthrough), a balance simulation, the AI Hub harness in four configurations, browser deep-link checks and screenshots. No subagents.\n- **Research:** the engine handoff docs, the sports kit, the AI Hub protocol and PLAN.md. No web research on hockey.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (headless Chromium used for checks).\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** session time roughly 1 h 30 min. API cost and token counts are unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 11, including AI checks that could never fire, goal records that lost their shot type, drills whose setup was overwritten, hub traffic that stopped during the countdown, and a draw-time crash in the KABOOM glow.\n- **How many were critical?** 4: no hits in AI play, drills starting in a faceoff, the hub host sending nothing during the card, and the KABOOM glow crash.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted story playthrough plus the AI Hub harness.\n- **Least helpful test:** screenshots from the slow software-rendered headless browser and the noisy 10-game balance averages. Headless logic tests also never exercise drawing.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most about the engine?** The fixed-step headless mode and the ready-made rigs, TileMap floors, lights, particles, scenes, Dialog and standard pause, settings and controls.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. `r.glowDisc` takes a canvas context first, which I got wrong. The Dialog `voice` option only takes an sfx name. The 5x7 font lacks arrows and check marks, and the tiny font lacks PlayStation symbols.\n- **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The whole hockey simulation, AI, netcode, replay and fight systems.\n- **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing hockey gear on a rig with no stick, skates or pads, and depth-sorting large custom board and glass panels.\n- **What did you change in the engine, and why?** I added PlayStation symbols to the font, made the gamepad ignore Options while Create is held, added `audio.bus()` with voice and crowd buses, and let a Dialog `voice` be a function.\n- **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** A documented way to add weapons, gear and extra joints to a Humanoid, and a public audio graph API.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most about this prompt?** The detailed plan and the clear TASK.md checklist.\n- **What was confusing?** The plan's file name and model differ from TASK.md's, and the plan asks for more than one session can deliver at full fidelity.\n- **What was the hardest thing to do?** Making every plan item real and playable in one sitting.\n- **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark must-have versus stretch items, give a code-size target, and say how to resolve plan-versus-TASK.md conflicts up front."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2899,"cache_read_input_tokens":536310,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2899},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de63938e-b4cc-4b63-8e8c-4cc91a6c7b2f","uuid":"1fb62f35-b895-4c63-b367-faf23cbecb02","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:03:46.522Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1i6MrRqCwGE8n4GYUg"}
