{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1mZLAm2Fg2bKWR6UcM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The goal horn now uses a real brass-style periodic wave (odd-harmonic-heavy, through the lowpass) instead of the plain sawtooth. I rebuilt, and the static and systems suites pass (10 and 20 checks, 0 failed). A browser run that fires the horn shows no errors. I did not re-run the full 130-check suite after this change; the last full run (before it) was 130 passed, 0 failed across 11 suites.\n\nI am not claiming \"every plan feature verified\". What I can show is the TASK.md checklist, covered by the tests and the screenshots. That includes the KABOOM, replay, flood and shootout screens and the fight HUD.\n\nWhat is not done is a custom `solvePose` skating and goalie animation layer. That is a PLAN.md detail, not a TASK.md requirement. The engine's own procedural run, shot, check, fall and fight poses are driven by the simulation state instead.\n\n`IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-055058.html` and `exit-interview.json` are in the work folder root; `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:50:58\n- **Source:** Ice hockey (over the top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports (3-on-3 with goalies, fight minigame, story campaign, exhibition, drills, online versus); 2.5D broadcast camera (engine `threequarter`) with Overhead and `brawler` views.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 patched in four places, plain JavaScript in one IIFE, AI Hub session client 1.4.0; Node `vm` and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** engine-native PS1-era pixel art with HD Humanoid rigs; hockey gear, logos, rink, boards, glass, stands and crowds drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural Humanoid rig driven by simulation state; no `solvePose` overrides.\n- **Audio:** all music, effects and voices synthesized in code, including Animalese-style babble voices, an organ drawbar wave and a brass-wave goal horn. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world, 1–4 players, host-authoritative with client prediction.\n- **Testing:** headless scripts (unit, systems, input, attract, dev, drills, full story playthrough), a balance simulation, the AI Hub harness in four configurations, browser deep-link checks and screenshots. No subagents.\n- **Research:** the engine handoff docs, the sports kit, the AI Hub protocol and PLAN.md. No web research on hockey.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (headless Chromium used for checks).\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** session time roughly 1 h 40 min. API cost and token counts are unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 11, including AI checks that could never fire, goal records that lost their shot type, drills whose setup was overwritten, hub traffic that stopped during the countdown, and a draw-time crash in the KABOOM glow.\n- **How many were critical?** 4: no hits in AI play, drills starting in a faceoff, the hub host sending nothing during the card, and the KABOOM glow crash.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted story playthrough plus the AI Hub harness.\n- **Least helpful test:** screenshots from the slow software-rendered headless browser and the noisy 10-game balance averages; headless logic tests never exercise drawing.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most about the engine?** The fixed-step headless mode and the ready-made rigs, TileMap floors, lights, particles, scenes, Dialog and standard pause, settings and controls.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes: `r.glowDisc` takes a canvas context first, Dialog `voice` only takes an sfx name, and the pixel fonts lack some symbols.\n- **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The whole hockey simulation, AI, netcode, replay and fight systems.\n- **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing hockey gear on a rig with no stick, skates or pads, and depth-sorting large custom board and glass panels.\n- **What did you change in the engine, and why?** Added PlayStation symbols to the font, made the gamepad ignore Options while Create is held, added `audio.bus()` with voice and crowd buses, and let a Dialog `voice` be a function.\n- **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** A documented way to add weapons, gear and extra joints to a Humanoid, and a public audio graph API.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most about this prompt?** The detailed plan and the clear TASK.md checklist.\n- **What was confusing?** The plan's file name and model differ from TASK.md's, and the plan asks for more than one session can deliver at full fidelity.\n- **What was the hardest thing to do?** Making every plan item real and playable in one sitting.\n- **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark must-have versus stretch items, give a code-size target, and say how to resolve plan-versus-TASK.md conflicts up front."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":296,"cache_read_input_tokens":542999,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":296},"output_tokens":798,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de63938e-b4cc-4b63-8e8c-4cc91a6c7b2f","uuid":"83b79e35-521b-4952-8ac2-4bf6eb4e38e3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:04:29.279Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1mZ1KRHeixi8aAzyMq"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The deliverables are present (the single HTML file in the work folder root, exit-interview.json parses with all fields filled, and the four feedback sections appear in the final reply), but the condition requires every feature in TASK.md to be implemented and verified. The last assistant message says the full 130-check suite was not re-run after the final brass-wave change, admits the planned custom solvePose skating/goalie animation layer was not built, and says it is not claiming every plan feature is verified. The transcript shows the KABOOM, replay, flood and shootout screens were checked only by error counts or a few screenshots, and the fight HUD and attract/dev/touch behavior were not visually verified. Test passes show logic works, not full feature completeness."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de63938e-b4cc-4b63-8e8c-4cc91a6c7b2f","uuid":"76a8d5f7-98ec-4ce1-b0e6-262cee055054","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:04:33.386Z","isSynthetic":true}
